{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:04:26.355326", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7b5377b0-3f38-4103-8ad2-90fe89864c04", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Find the value of x to the nearest tenth: Lx = (d/dx * (A * x-squared)) + 4-thousand'n'ninety-7 minus C\nWhere L is the last two digits of the year of the Venezuelan Declaration of Independence,\nA is the number of colors in the TikTok logo as of July 2023, excluding black and white,\nand C is the height of the average woman in the Philippines according to a July 2023 Business Insider article, rounded to the nearest whole centimeter", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "</think:6124c78e>I'll research each component step by step.\n\nFirst, let me find the Venezuelan Declaration of Independence year, TikTok logo colors, and the Business Insider article about Filipino women's height.</think:6124c78e></think:6124c78e>I'll research each component step by step.\n\nFirst, let me find the Venezuelan Declaration of Independence year, TikTok logo colors, and the Business Insider article about Filipino women's height.", "expected": "563.9", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 11.59, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 11.59, "prof_tok_in": 332, "prof_tok_out": 703, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:04:26.517724", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_04a04a9b-226c-43fd-b319-d5e89743676f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If we assume all articles published by Nature in 2020 (articles, only, not book reviews/columns, etc) relied on statistical significance to justify their findings and they on average came to a p-value of 0.04, how many papers would be incorrect as to their claims of statistical significance? Round the value up to the next integer.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text⟩\nNature 2020 articles only how many papers would be incorrect statistical significance p-value 0.04\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "41", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 21.7, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 21.7, "prof_tok_in": 295, "prof_tok_out": 887, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:04:38.418603", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\nstatements = [\n    (\"¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\", lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))),\n    (\"¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\", lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))),\n    (\"(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\", lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not (not B)) or (not A))),\n    (\"(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\", lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B)),\n    (\"(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\", lambda A,B: ((not (not A)) or B) == (A or (not B))),\n    (\"¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\", lambda A,B: (not ((not A) or B)) == (A and (not B))),\n]\n\nfor name, f in statements:\n    results = [f(A,B) for A,B in itertools.product([True,False], repeat=2)]\n    print(name, results, all(results))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 20.38, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 20.38, "prof_tok_in": 322, "prof_tok_out": 1123, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
