{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:11:50.636876", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_ad2b4d70-9314-4fe6-bfbe-894a45f6055f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Eva Draconis has a personal website which can be accessed on her YouTube page. What is the meaning of the only symbol seen in the top banner that has a curved line that isn't a circle or a portion of a circle? Answer without punctuation.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\nEva Draconis personal website YouTube page top banner symbol meaning curved line not circle", "expected": "War is not here this is a land of peace", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 20.84, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 20.84, "prof_tok_in": 274, "prof_tok_out": 140, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:11:50.771989", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_983bba7c-c092-455f-b6c9-7857003d48fc", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: What animals that were mentioned in both Ilias Lagkouvardos's and Olga Tapia's papers on the alvei species of the genus named for Copenhagen outside the bibliographies were also present in the 2021 article cited on the alvei species' Wikipedia page about a multicenter, randomized, double-blind study?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search_1\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Hafnia alvei Wikipedia 2021 multicenter randomized double-blind study</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "mice", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 23.67, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 23.67, "prof_tok_in": 290, "prof_tok_out": 408, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:11:53.106067", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    \"1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"3\": lambda A,B: ((A implies B) if False else (not A or B)) == ((not B implies not A) if False else (B or not A)),\n    # Let's just implement directly\n}\n\n# Actually implement properly\ndef f1(A,B):\n    return (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\ndef f2(A,B):\n    return (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\ndef f3(A,B):\n    return ((not A) or B) == (B or (not A))  # A->B = ¬A∨B; ¬B->¬A = B∨¬A, same\ndef f4(A,B):\n    return ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B)\ndef f5(A,B):\n    # (¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n    left = (not (not A)) or B  # ¬A→B = A ∨ B\n    right = A or (not B)\n    return left == right\ndef f6(A,B):\n    # ¬(A→B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n    left = not ((not A) or B)\n    right = A and (not B)\n    return left == right\n\nfor name,f in [(\"1\",f1),(\"2\",f2),(\"3\",f3),(\"4\",f4),(\"5\",f5),(\"6\",f6)]:\n    results = [f(A,B) for A in [True,False] for B in [True,False]]\n    print(name, results, all(results))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 24.98, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 24.98, "prof_tok_in": 322, "prof_tok_out": 1200, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
