{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:13:31.992651", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_46719c30-f4c3-4cad-be07-d5cb21eee6bb", "task_desc": "Among the authors (First M. Last format) who contributed to the 2015 paper \"Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better?\", identify the one who had published papers before that. Then, give the title of that author's earliest paper.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [1 @v51] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>query>Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better? 2015 authors</query>\n<num_results>10</num_results>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query>Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better? 2015 authors</query>\n<num_results>10\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Mapping Human Oriented Information to Software Agents for Online Systems Usage", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 409, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 56.12, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 56.12, "prof_tok_in": 353, "prof_tok_out": 144, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:13:33.456000", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, please report the longest word that comes first, alphabetically. Oh, and I know that there might be differen", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport requests\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# Download words_alpha dictionary\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nresp = requests.get(url)\nwords = resp.text.split()\nprint(\"Dictionary size:\", len(words))\n\n# Build set and prefix set\nword_set = set(w.strip().lower() for w in words if w.isalpha())\nprefix_set = set()\nfor w in word_set:\n    for i in range(1, len(w)+1):\n        prefix_set.add(w[:i])\n\n# Board\nboard = [\n    ['a','b','r','l'],\n    ['e','i','t','e'],\n    ['i','o','n','s'],\n    ['f','p','e','i']\n]\nrows = 4\ncols = 4\n\n# DFS\nfound = set()\n\ndef dfs(r, c, path, visited):\n    letter = board[r][c]\n    path += letter\n    if path not in prefix_set:\n        return\n    if len(path) >= 3 and path in word_set:\n        found.add(path)\n    # explore neighbors\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr==0 and dc==0:\n                continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                visited.add((nr,nc))\n                dfs(nr, nc, path, visited)\n                visited.remove((nr,nc))\n\nfor r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n        visited = {(r,c)}\n        dfs(r, c, \"\", visited)\n\n# Find longest\nmax_len = max(len(w) for w in found)\nlongest = sorted([w for w in found if len(w)==max_len])\nprint(\"Max length:\", max_len)\nprint(\"Count of longest:\", len(longest))\nprint(\"First alphabetically:\", longest[0] if longest else None)\nprint(\"All longest:\", longest[:20])\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 60.0, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 60.0, "prof_tok_in": 362, "prof_tok_out": 1047, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
