{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:13:36.705635", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_42576abe-0deb-4869-8c63-225c2d75a95a", "task_desc": "In the constructed language Tizin, basic sentence structure follows Verb → Direct Object → Subject order. You want to tell your Tizin-speaking friend that you enjoy apples.\n\nThe first-person pronoun takes these forms: \"Pa\" (nominative), \"Mato\" (accusative), and \"Sing\" (genitive).\n\nThe verb root for strong liking is \"Maktay.\" In the present tense it stays in root form; for the preterit past it becomes \"Tay\"; for the imperfect past it becomes \"Aktay.\" Crucially, its usage differs from English — it", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [1 @v45] Maktay Mato Apple:  -> Maktay Mato Apple (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "Maktay Mato Apple", "expected": "Maktay mato apple", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 171, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 66.08, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 66.08, "prof_tok_in": 459, "prof_tok_out": 1212, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
