{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:13:39.562592", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Here is the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nYour job is to answer the following question precisely.\n\nQuestion: Among the statements below, exactly one is **not** logically equivalent to the others:\n\n¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nIdentify the full statement that does not belong.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [1 @v36] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    \"1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"3\": lambda A,B: ((A implies B) if False else (not A or B)) == ((not B implies not A) if False else (B or not A)),\n    # Let's just implement directly\n}\n\n# Actually implement properly\ndef f1(A,B):\n    return (not (A and B)) == ((no (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef truth_table(formula):\n    vals = []\n    for A,B in itertools.product([False,True], repeat=2):\n        vals.append(formula(A,B))\n    return vals\n\nS1 = lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\nS2 = lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\nS3 = lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ( (not (not B)) or (not A) )  # A->B == notB->notA\n# Actually A->B = not A or B; notB->notA = not(not B) or not A = B or not A, same.\nS4 = lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B)\nS5 = lambda A,B: ( (not (not A)) or B ) == ( A or (not B) )  # (¬A→B) == A∨B; RHS A∨¬B\nS6 = lambda A,B: (not ((not A) or B)) == (A and (not B))\n\nfor name,S in [(\"S1\",S1),(\"S2\",S2),(\"S3\",S3),(\"S4\",S4),(\"S5\",S5),(\"S6\",S6)]:\n    print(name, truth_table(S))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 554, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 70.63, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 70.63, "prof_tok_in": 511, "prof_tok_out": 1697, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
