{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:14:15.277042", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b7f857e4-d8aa-4387-af2a-0e844df5b9d8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached image contains a Python script. Run the Python code against an array of strings, listed below. The output of the Python script will be a URL containing C++ source code. Compile and run this C++ code against the array [35, 12, 8, 99, 21, 5] and return the sum of the third and fifth integers in the sorted list.\n\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jkl', 'tps', '/Q', 'pqr', 'stu', ':', '//', 'rose', 'vwx', 'yz1', '234', 'tta', '567', '890'", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport requests, re, textwrap, sys, json, os\n\nurl = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort#C++\"\ntry:\n    r = requests.get(url, timeout=20)\n    print(\"status\", r.status_code)\n    # print a snippet around C++\n    text = r.text\n    idx = text.find(\"C++\")\n    print(text[idx-200:idx+500])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error\", e)\n```", "expected": "47", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 146.61, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 146.61, "prof_tok_in": 420, "prof_tok_out": 7233, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
