{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:15:24.861274", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_08cae58d-4084-4616-b6dd-dd6534e4825b", "task_desc": "Based on the data from Google Finance, in what year did Apple's stock price first exceed $50 per share (using unadjusted prices, i.e., not accounting for stock splits)?", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v159] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search`\nquery`:`Apple stock historical price first time above $50 Google Finance unadjusted`\n`</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v77] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search`\nquery`:`Apple stock historical price first time above $50 Google Finance`\n`</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search`\nquery`:`Apple stock historical price first time above $50 Google Finance unadjusted`\n`</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "2018", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 610, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 62.2, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 62.2, "prof_tok_in": 371, "prof_tok_out": 115, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:15:26.293448", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Among the following, identify the one statement that is not logically equivalent to the others:\n\n¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above does not belong? Give the complete statement that differs.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [1 @v36] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    \"1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"3\": lambda A,B: ((A implies B) if False else (not A or B)) == ((not B implies not A) if False else (B or not A)),\n    # Let's just implement directly\n}\n\n# Actually implement properly\ndef f1(A,B):\n    return (not (A and B)) == ((no (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [1 @v140] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef truth_table(formula):\n    vals = []\n    for A,B in itertools.product([False,True], repeat=2):\n        vals.append(formula(A,B))\n    return vals\n\nS1 = lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\nS2 = lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\nS3 = lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ( (not (not B)) or (not A) )  # A->B == notB->notA\n# Actually A->B = not A (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef f1(A,B): return (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\ndef f2(A,B): return (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\ndef f3(A,B): return ((A or (not B)) if False else (not A or B)) == ((not (not B)) or (not A)) # wait implement properly\n# Let's implement directly:\ndef impl(A,B): return (not A) or B\ndef f3(A,B): return impl(A,B) == impl(not B, not A)\ndef f4(A,B): return impl(A,B) == ((not A) or B)\ndef f5(A,B): return impl(not A, B) == (A or (not B))\ndef f6(A,B): return (not impl(A,B)) == (A and (not B))\n\nfor name,f in [('1',f1),('2',f2),('3',f3),('4',f4),('5',f5),('6',f6)]:\n    vals = [f(A,B) for A,B in itertools.product([False,True], repeat=2)]\n    print(name, vals, all(vals))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 1029, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 74.69, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 74.69, "prof_tok_in": 660, "prof_tok_out": 807, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
