{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:15:27.994066", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4d0aa727-86b1-406b-9b33-f870dd14a4a5", "task_desc": "Here is the reworded task:\n\nThe accompanying file catalogs the locomotive roster of a regional railroad museum. For each locomotive, it provides the identification number, whether it is currently in service, and—if it is operational—the name of the daily excursion it pulls. If every daily excursion selects one of its assigned locomotives uniformly at random, what are the chances that today's Sunset Picnic Trip will be hauled by a steam locomotive? Express your answer in the format \"1 in 4\", \"1 i", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v70] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport os\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\n``` (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v155] [AVOID] </think:6124c78e>```python:  -> </think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\n``` (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport glob, os\nprint(glob.glob('*'))\n```", "expected": "1 in 3", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 355, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 70.15, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 70.15, "prof_tok_in": 424, "prof_tok_out": 700, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
