{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:15:37.123916", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_72c06643-a2fa-4186-aa5c-9ec33ae9b445", "task_desc": "Determine the following value precisely.\n\nQuestion: Suppose you have 0.312 kg of Freon-12 refrigerant placed at the deepest point of the Marianas Trench, where it equilibrates to the highest temperature found at that depth. Compute the system's volume in milliliters and round to the nearest whole milliliter. Return only an integer.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [3 @v65] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tmoved to bottom of Marianas Trench Freon-12 0.312 kg volume milliliters\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [3 @v158] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tMarianas Trench bottom maximum temperature pressure\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tFreon-12 liquid density kg/m3 at 4 C pressure\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tMarianas Trench bottom highest temperature found at that depth\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tFreon-12 liquid density kg/m3 at 4 C\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tChallenger Deep pressure MPa temperature Celsius\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "55", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 700, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 75.67, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 75.67, "prof_tok_in": 432, "prof_tok_out": 1110, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:15:37.372362", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-separated list of countries in alphabetical order. Use the countries most common names in english when answering.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport requests, json, time\n\nind = 'NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS'\nurl = f'http://api.worldbank.org/v2/countries/all/indicators/{ind}'\nparams = {'date':'2001:2010','format':'json','per_page':1000,'page':1}\nall_rows = []\nwhile True:\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    data = r.json()\n    if len(data)<2:\n        break\n    meta = data[0]\n    rows = data[1]\n    if not rows:\n        break\n    all_rows.extend(rows)\n    pages = meta['pages']\n    if params['page'] >= pages:\n        break\n    params['page'] += 1\n    time.sleep(0.2)\nlen(all_rows)\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's inspect a sample row and structure\nall_rows[0]\n```\n\n```python\n# Get country metadata to distinguish aggregates\nc_url='http://api.worldbank.org/v2/countries?format=json&per_page=1000'\ncdata=requests.get(c_url).json()\ncountries_meta={c['id']:c for c in cdata[1]}\n# sample\nlist(countries_meta.items())[0]\n```\n\n```python\n# Filter rows with value not None, and collect by country\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ndata_by_country=defaultdict(dict)\nfor row in all_rows:\n    c=row['country']['id']\n    yr=row['date']\n    val=row['value']\n    if val is not None:\n        data_by_country[c][yr]=val\n\n# Need years 2001-2010 inclusive\nyears=[str(y) for y in range(2001,2011)]\nqualifying=[]\nfor c, d in data_by_country.items():\n    if all(y in d and d[y] > 35 for y in years):\n        # exclude aggregates? check metadata\n        meta=countries_meta.get(c)\n        if meta and meta.get('region') and 'Aggregates' not in meta['region']['value']:\n            qualifying.append((meta['name'], c))\nlen(qualifying), qualifying[:10]\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's see all qualifying with names\nnames=sorted([n for n,c in qualifying])\nnames\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's double-check if any aggregate slipped or if we need common English names. Print with iso and region\nfor n,c in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x:x[0]):\n    print(n, c, countries_meta[c]['region']['value'])\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also verify by checking values for a few countries to ensure >35 each year\nfor c in ['CHN','SGP','NOR','IDN','MYS','TKM','VNM','IRN','BRN','QAT','SAU','RUS','KAZ','AZE','TGO','BHR','UZB','KWT','ARE','OMN','MAC','HKG','TWN?']:\n    pass\n# Actually let's print the yearly values for the qualifying list to verify\nfor n,c in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x:x[0]):\n    vals=[data_by_country[c].get(y) for y in years]\n    print(n, vals)\n```\n\n```python\n# The list seems large. Need ensure we only include countries (not areas like Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan? World Bank includes as economies; question says countries. \"countries most common names in english\". Need decide whether to include economies like Hong Kong SAR, China; Macao SAR, China; Taiwan? World Bank API may list Taiwan, China as aggregate? Let's check. Also need check if some names should be simplified: \"China\", \"Singapore\", etc.\n# Let's get exact World Bank names for qualifying list.\n[name for name,_ in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x:x[0])]\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's inspect if any entries are not sovereign states: Hong Kong SAR, China; Macao SAR, China; Taiwan (maybe not in API). Also possibly \"Korea, Rep.\" should be \"South Korea\"? The question says countries most common names in english. We need map World Bank names to common English names.\n# Let's list all qualifying with their world bank name and iso2.\nfor n,c in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x:x[0]):\n    print(c, n)\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also fetch from World Bank the indicator via different source? Maybe the API data is correct. But we should verify with another source or ensure no missing data due to API gaps. Let's count how many countries had data for all years. Could there be countries with >35 but missing some year (so excluded). That's fine.\n# Need final list in alphabetical order using common English names. Let's map:\n# World Bank names observed:\n# Azerbaijan\n# Bahrain\n# Brunei Darussalam -> Brunei\n# China\n# Hong Kong SAR, China -> Hong Kong? But is it a country? The question says countries. Usually Hong Kong is not a country. But World Bank treats as economy. The question likely expects sovereign countries? Need infer from similar questions. \"countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year\" from World Bank data. Many such data queries include economies. But they ask \"countries\" and \"most common names in english\". They might expect \"China, Hong Kong, Macao, Singapore...\"? Hmm.\n# Let's see full list first.\n```\n\n```python\n# Print all\nfor n,c in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x:x[0]):\n    print(c, n)\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also check if there are any with exactly 35? We used >35 strict. Good.\n# Need to ensure years 2001-2010 inclusive. Some countries may have data only for some years; we required all. Good.\n# Let's also verify using the World Bank CSV download? Could be more reliable. But API seems fine.\n# Let's output the list of World Bank names sorted.\nwb_names=sorted([n for n,c in qualifying])\nwb_names\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also check if there is a separate indicator \"Gross savings (% of GDP)\" from World Bank's \"World Development Indicators\". Yes NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS. Good.\n# Now mapping to common English names:\n# Azerbaijan -> Azerbaijan\n# Bahrain -> Bahrain\n# Brunei Darussalam -> Brunei\n# China -> China\n# Hong Kong SAR, China -> Hong Kong (if included)\n# Indonesia -> Indonesia\n# Iran, Islamic Rep.