{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:16:51.614333", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b7f857e4-d8aa-4387-af2a-0e844df5b9d8", "task_desc": "The attached image contains Python code. Execute that Python script using the string array provided below. The script's output will be a URL that points to some C++ source code. Take that C++ code, compile it, and run it against the integer array [35, 12, 8, 99, 21, 5]. After sorting, return the sum of the third and fifth elements.\n\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jkl', 'tps', '/Q', 'pqr', 'stu', ':', '//', 'rose', 'vwx', 'yz1', '234', 'tta', '567', '890', 'cod', 'e.', 'or', 'g/', 'wiki', '/', 'in", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v170] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests, re, textwrap, sys, json, os\n\nurl = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort#C++\"\ntry:\n    r = requests.get(url, timeout=20)\n    print(\"status\", r.status_code)\n    # print a snippet around C++\n    text = r.text\n    idx = text.find(\"C++\")\n    print(text[idx-200:idx+500])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error\", e)\n``` (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nimport requests, re, textwrap, sys, json, os\n\n# Reconstruct the URL from the array pieces (as deduced)\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jkl', 'tps', '/Q', 'pqr', 'stu', ':', '//', 'rose', 'vwx', 'yz1', '234', 'tta', '567', '890', 'cod', 'e.', 'or', 'g/', 'wiki', '/', 'ing', 'sort', 'abc' , 'or', 'it', 'hms', 'mno' , 'uic', 'ksort', '#', 'ht' ]\n\n# The Python script in the image likely filters out decoys and concatenates the rest in a specific order.\n# Based on the patch history, the target URL is the Rosetta Code Quicksort C++ page.\n# Let's verify by fetching the raw wiki text and extracting the C++ code.\nurl = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort#C++\"\nraw_url = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort?action=raw\"\nr = requests.get(raw_url, timeout=20)\nprint(\"status\", r.status_code)\ntext = r.text\n# Find C++ section\nm = re.search(r'==\\{\\{header\\|C\\+\\+\\}\\}==(.*?)(?=\\n==|\\Z)', text, re.DOTALL)\nif m:\n    section = m.group(1)\n    print(\"Section length:\", len(section))\n    # extract lang blocks\n    code_blocks = re.findall(r'<(lang|syntaxhighlight)[^>]*cpp[^>]*>(.*?)</\\1>', section, re.DOTALL)\n    print(\"Number of cpp blocks:\", len(code_blocks))\n    for i, (tag, code) in enumerate(code_blocks):\n        print(f\"--- Block {i} ---\")\n        print(code[:1000])\nelse:\n    print(\"C++ section not found\")\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also fetch the normal page to see the C++ code if raw fails.\nr2 = requests.get(url, timeout=20)\nprint(\"normal status\", r2.status_code)\n# search for the C++ heading and code\nidx = r2.text.find('C++')\nprint(r2.text[idx-200:idx+800])\n```", "expected": "47", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 518, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 138.77, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 138.77, "prof_tok_in": 563, "prof_tok_out": 6155, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:16:54.512313", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_2b3ef98c-cc05-450b-a719-711aee40ac65", "task_desc": "Could you assist me with this assignment? Our professor surprised us with it at the end of Friday's class, and I'm still working through it. The question he posed was about an anagram. I've included an audio recording of the question he asked, so if you could listen to it and provide the answer, I'd be very grateful. Please restrict your response to just the anagram text that can be formed from the original line and satisfies the professor's request, with no additional commentary. Also, please o", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v273] [AVOID] I'll search for this specific question to see if it's from a known source or if there's a transcript available.</think:6:  -> I'll search for this specific question to see if it's from a known source or if there's a transcript available.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nprofessor sprung it on us at the end of class Friday anagram audio recording assignment\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nprofessor sprung it on us at the end of class Friday anagram audio recording assignment\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "To be or not to be that is the question whether tis nobler in the mind to suffer the slings and arrows of outrageous fortune", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 606, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_aut