{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:16:56.497661", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7cc4acfa-63fd-4acc-a1a1-e8e529e0a97f", "task_desc": "Here is the reworded task:\n\n---\n\nUsing the provided spreadsheet that records menu-item sales for a regional fast-food chain, determine which of the two cities—Wharvton or Algrimand—generated the higher total sales.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v271] [AVOID] I'll search for information about these cities and the spreadsheet mentioned.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> I'll search for information about these cities and the spreadsheet mentioned.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\nquery\n=\"Wharvton\" \"Algrimand\" sales menu items fast-food\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v275] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\nquery\n=\"Wharvton\" \"Algrimand\" spreadsheet\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\nquery\n=\"Wharvton\" \"Algrimand\" \"fast-food\"\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\nquery\n=\"Wharvton\" \"Algrimand\"\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Wharvton", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 830, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 4.25, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 4.25, "prof_tok_in": 430, "prof_tok_out": 247, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:16:57.567927", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_08f3a05f-5947-4089-a4c4-d4bcfaa6b7a0", "task_desc": "Starting with $x_0 = -5$ and the function $f(x) = x^3 + 4x^2 - 3x + 8$, determine the minimum number of iterations $n$ required for Newton's Method to satisfy $x_{n+1} = x_n$ once both are rounded to four decimal places.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v232] Starting with the initial value $x_0 = -5$ and the function $f(x) = x^3 + 4x^2 - 3x + 8$, apply Newton's Method and roun:  -> Starting with the initial value $x_0 = -5$ and the function $f(x) = x^3 + 4x^2 - 3x + 8$, apply Newton's Method and round to four decimal places after each iteration. Determine the smallest integer $n$ for which the iteration satisfies $n = n + 1$. (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v81] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code_execution<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code_text>\nimport decimal\nfrom decimal import Decimal, getcontext\ngetcontext().prec = 50\n\ndef f(x):\n    return x**3 + 4*x**2 - 3*x + 8\ndef fp(x):\n    return 3*x**2 + 8*x - 3\n\nx = Decimal(-5)\nfor i in range(10):\n    fx = f(x)\n    fpx = fp(x)\n    x_new = x - fx/fpx\n    print(i, x, x_new, round(float(x), (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code_execution<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code_text>\nimport math\n\ndef f(x):\n    return x**3 + 4*x**2 - 3*x + 8\ndef fp(x):\n    return 3*x**2 + 8*x - 3\n\ndef newton_round(use_rounded_as_input=True, max_iter=20):\n    x = -5.0\n    hist = [round(x,4)]\n    x_prev = x\n    for i in range(max_iter):\n        if use_rounded_as_input:\n            x_in = hist[-1]\n        else:\n            x_in = x_prev\n        x_next = x_in - f(x_in)/fp(x_in)\n        x_next_r = round(x_next,4)\n        hist.append(x_next_r)\n        x_prev = x_next\n        if x_next_r == hist[-2]:\n            return i+1, hist  # n? i+1 is index of next? Let's track\n    return None, hist\n\nprint('rounded input:')\nn, hist = newton_round(True, 20)\nprint(n, hist)\nprint('exact input but compare rounded:')\nn2, hist2 = newton_round(False, 20)\nprint(n2, hist2)\n</parameter>\n</invoke>\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code_text>\nimport math\n\ndef f(x):\n    return x**3 + 4*x**2 - 3*x + 8\ndef fp(x):\n    return 3*x**2 + 8*x - 3\n\ndef newton_round(use_rounded_as_input=True, max_iter=20):\n    x = -5.0\n    hist = [round(x,4)]\n    x_prev = x\n    for i in range(max_iter):\n        if use_rounded_as_input:\n            x_in = hist[-1]\n        else:\n            x_in = x_prev\n        x_next = x_in - f(x_in)/fp(x_in)\n        x_next_r = round(x_next,4)\n        hist.append(x_next_r)\n        x_prev = x_next\n        if x_next_r == hist[-2]:\n            return i+1, hist\n    return None, hist\n\nprint('rounded input:')\nn, hist = newton_round(True, 20)\nprint(n, hist)\nprint('exact input but compare rounded:')\nn2, hist2 = newton_round(False, 20)\nprint(n2, hist2)\n</parameter>\n</invoke>", "expected": "2", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 984, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 19.16, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 19.16, "prof_tok_in": 581, "prof_tok_out": 1020, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:17:01.408006", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7dd30055-0198-452e-8c25-f73dbe27dcb8", "task_desc": "Using Biopython in Python, retrieve and parse the protein structure corresponding to PDB ID 5wb7 from the RCSB Protein Data Bank. Compute the Euclidean distance separating the first atom and the second atom according to their order in the PDB file. Provide the result in Angstroms, rounded to the nearest picometer.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v265] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests, math\nfrom Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n\npdb_id = \"5wb7\"\nurl = f\"https://files.rcsb.org/download/{pdb_id}.pdb\"\nr = requests.get(url)\nopen(f\"{pdb_id}.pdb\",\"w\").write(r.text)\n\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure(pdb_id, f\"{pdb_id}.pdb\")\n\n# atoms in file order as yielded by Biopython\natoms = list(structure.get_atoms())\na1, a2 = atoms[0], atoms[1]\nc1,  (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v127] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport sys, subprocess, json, os, math, textwrap, io\n\n# Ensure biopython is available\ntry:\n    import Bio\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"biopython\", \"-q\"])\n\nfrom Bio.PDB import PDBParser\nimport requests\n\npdb_id = \"5wb7\"\nurl = f\"https://files.rcsb.org/download/{pdb_id}.pdb\"\nr = requests.get(url)\nprint(\"status\", r.status_code, \"len\", (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nimport sys, subprocess, json, os, math\ntry:\n    from Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n    import requests\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"biopython\", \"-q\"])\n    from Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n    import requests\n\npdb_id = \"5wb7\"\nurl = f\"https://files.rcsb.org/download/{pdb_id}.pdb\"\nr = requests.get(url)\nopen(f\"{pdb_id}.pdb\",\"w\").write(r.text)\n\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure(pdb_id, f\"{pdb_id}.pdb\")\n\natoms = list(structure.get_atoms())\na1, a2 = atoms[0], atoms[1]\ncoord1 = a1.get_coord()\ncoord2 = a2.get_coord()\ndist = math.sqrt(sum((c1-c2)**2 for c1,c2 in zip(coord1, coord2)))\n# round to nearest picometer: 1 pm = 0.01 Angstrom\ndist_pm = round(dist * 100)  # in pm\ndist_rounded_ang = dist_pm / 100.0\nprint(\"first atom:\", a1.get_parent().id, a1.id, a1.element)\nprint(\"second atom:\", a2.get_parent().id, a2.id, a2.element)\nprint(\"distance A:\", dist)\nprint(\"rounded A to nearest pm:\", dist_rounded_ang)\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also verify by reading raw PDB lines to ensure order matches\nwith open(f\"{pdb_id}.pdb\") as f:\n    lines = [l for l in f if l.startswith((\"ATOM\",\"HETATM\"))]\nprint(\"first two atom lines:\")\nprint(lines[0])\nprint(lines[1])\n# parse coords manually\ndef parse_coord(line):\n    return (float(line[30:38]), float(line[38:46]), float(line[46:54]))\nc1 = parse_coord(lines[0])\nc2 = parse_coord(lines[1])\nd2 = math.sqrt(sum((x-y)**2 for x,y in zip(c1,c2)))\nprint(\"manual distance A:\", d2)\nprint(\"manual rounded A:\", round(d2*100)/100)\n```", "expected": "1.456", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 1014, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.85, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 11.35, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 11.35, "prof_tok_in": 594, "prof_tok_out": 766, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
