{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:17:49.628448", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_14569e28-c88c-43e4-8c32-097d35b9a67d", "task_desc": "In Unlambda, what specific character or text must be inserted to fix the code below so that it prints \"For penguins\"? If a character is required, respond with the character's name. When multiple names exist for the same character, use the briefest one. You do not need to indicate where the text goes. Code:\n\n`r```````````.F.o.r. .p.e.n.g.u.i.n.si`", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v272] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Unlambda \"For penguins\" code</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v144] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Unlambda \"For penguins\" code</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e> (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_sep:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</arg_key:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Unlambda \"For penguins\" code</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "backtick", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 690, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 13.03, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 13.03, "prof_tok_in": 415, "prof_tok_out": 866, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:18:06.153495", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nHere's a Boggle board I've set up:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nWhat's the longest English word you can form from this board? I want to know the longest word that can be generated from it. If there's a tie at the maximum length, give me the one that sorts first alphabetically. And since different Boggle word lists exist, let's stick to the words_alpha dictionary hosted at https://github.com/dwyl/english-words as our official word source.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [3 @v269] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# Download words_alpha dictionary\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nresp = requests.get(url)\nwords = resp.text.split()\nprint(\"Dictionary size:\", len(words))\n\n# Build set and prefix set\nword_set = set(w.strip().lower() for w in words if w.isalpha())\nprefix_set = set()\nfor w in word_set:\n (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [3 @v132] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# Download words_alpha dictionary\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nresp = requests.get(url)\nwords = resp.text.split()\nprint(\"Dictionary size:\", len(words))\n\n# Build set and prefix set\nword_set = set(w.strip().lower() for w in words if w.isalpha())\nprefix_set = set()\nfor w in word_set:\n (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nimport requests\n\n# Download dictionary\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nresp = requests.get(url)\nwords = resp.text.split()\nword_set = set(w.strip().lower() for w in words if w.isalpha())\n# prefix set for pruning\nprefix_set = set()\nfor w in word_set:\n    for i in range(1, len(w)+1):\n        prefix_set.add(w[:i])\n\n# Boggle board\nboard = [\n    ['a','b','r','l'],\n    ['e','i','t','e'],\n    ['i','o','n','s'],\n    ['f','p','e','i']\n]\nrows = 4\ncols = 4\n\nfound = set()\n\ndef dfs(r, c, path, visited):\n    letter = board[r][c]\n    word = path + letter\n    if word not in prefix_set:\n        return\n    if word in word_set:\n        found.add(word)\n    # explore neighbors\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                visited.add((nr,nc))\n                dfs(nr, nc, word, visited)\n                visited.remove((nr,nc))\n\nfor r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n        visited = {(r,c)}\n        dfs(r,c,\"\",visited)\n\n# find longest\nmax_len = max(len(w) for w in found)\nlongest = sorted([w for w in found if len(w)==max_len])\nprint(\"Max length:\", max_len)\nprint(\"Count of longest:\", len(longest))\nprint(\"First few alphabetically:\", longest[:10])\nprint(\"Longest words:\", longest)\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 1014, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 17.86, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 17.86, "prof_tok_in": 577, "prof_tok_out": 1174, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:18:07.831007", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7b5377b0-3f38-4103-8ad2-90fe89864c04", "task_desc": "Compute the value of x and round it to the nearest tenth: Lx = (d/dx * (A * x²)) + 4097 − C\n\nwhere:\n- L equals the final two digits of the year Venezuela issued its Declaration of Independence,\n- A equals the count of colors in the TikTok logo as of July 2023 (do not count black or white),\n- and C equals the mean height of a woman in the Philippines, in centimeters rounded to the nearest whole number, as reported in a July 2023 Business Insider article.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v286] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nVenezuelan Declaration of Independence year</think:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nTikTok logo colors excluding black and white July 2023 number of colors</arg_value:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nBusiness Insider July 2023 average woman height Ph (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v288] [AVOID] <tool_calls:6124c78e>:  -> <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nVenezuela declared independence year July 5 1811 final two digits (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nVenezuela Declaration of Independence year July 5 1811 final two digits\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nTikTok logo colors excluding black white July 2023 count\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\nBusiness Insider July 2023 average woman height Philippines centimeters rounded whole number\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "563.9", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 799, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 8.64, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 8.64, "prof_tok_in": 486, "prof_tok_out": 520, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:18:11.321937", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Please answer the following question precisely.\n\nQuestion: Per World Bank data, for each year from 2001 through 2010, which nations maintained gross savings exceeding 35% of their GDP? Provide your response as a comma-separated list, sorted alphabetically, using each country's most common English name.", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v276] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests, json, time\n\nind = 'NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS'\nurl = f'http://api.worldbank.org/v2/countries/all/indicators/{ind}'\nparams = {'date':'2001:2010','format':'json','per_page':1000,'page':1}\nall_rows = []\nwhile True:\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    data = r.json()\n    if len(data)<2:\n        break\n    meta = data[0]\n    rows = data[1]\n    if not rows:\n        break\n    all_r (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v252] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests, json, time\n\nind = 'NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS'\nurl = f'http://api.worldbank.org/v2/countries/all/indicators/{ind}'\nparams = {'date':'2001:2010','format':'json','per_page':1000,'page':1}\nall_rows = []\nwhile True:\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    data = r.json()\n    if len(data)<2:\n        break\n    meta = data[0]\n    rows = data[1]\n    if not rows:\n        break\n    all_r (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nimport requests, json, time\n\n# Get list of countries (exclude aggregates)\nc_url = 'http://api.worldbank.org/v2/countries'\nc_params = {'format':'json','per_page':1000}\nr = requests.get(c_url, params=c_params)\ncdata = r.json()[1]\ncountry_codes = {}\nfor c in cdata:\n    if c['region']['value'] != 'Aggregates':\n        country_codes[c['id']] = c['name']\n\n# Indicator for gross savings (% of GDP)\nind = 'NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS'\nurl = f'http://api.worldbank.org/v2/countries/all/indicators/{ind}'\nparams = {'date':'2001:2010','format':'json','per_page':1000,'page':1}\nall_rows = []\nwhile True:\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    data = r.json()\n    if len(data) < 2:\n        break\n    rows = data[1]\n    if not rows:\n        break\n    all_rows.extend(rows)\n    if len(rows) < params['per_page']:\n        break\n    params['page'] += 1\n\n# Organize by country\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nby_country = defaultdict(dict)\nfor row in all_rows:\n    code = row['countryiso3code']\n    cname = row['country']['value']\n    year = int(row['date'])\n    val = row['value']\n    if val is not None:\n        by_country[(code,cname)][year] = val\n\n# Filter countries with >35 for all years 2001-2010\nresult = []\nfor (code,cname), yvals in by_country.items():\n    if code not in country_codes:\n        continue\n    if all(year in yvals and yvals[year] > 35 for year in range(2001,2011)):\n        result.append(cname)\n\nresult_sorted = sorted(result)\nprint(len(result_sorted))\nprint(result_sorted)\n```", "expected": "Brunei, China, Morocco, Singapore", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 1030, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 6.76, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 6.76, "prof_tok_in": 599, "prof_tok_out": 999, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:18:15.720949", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_56db2318-640f-477a-a82f-bc93ad13e882", "task_desc": "The following numbers operate similarly to ISBN-13 numbers but with a different validation scheme. Instead of alternating weights of 1 and 3, the checksum digit uses a weight of 1 alternating with some other positive integer below 10. Apart from that, the checksum digit is computed in the usual way. Unfortunately, the data contains an error: two adjacent columns have been swapped. The swapped columns do not involve the last column nor any of the first three columns. Using this information, deter", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [3 @v264] ```python:  -> ```python\nrows_str = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\nrows = [[int(ch) for ch in s] for s in rows_str]\n\nsolutions = []\n# w from 2 to 9 (positive integer below 10, other than 1 and 3? include 3 just in case)\nfor w in rang (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [3 @v118] ```python:  -> ```python\n# Let's define the digits for each row\nrows_str = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\n\nrows = [[int(ch) for ch in s] for s in rows_str]\nprint(len(rows), [len(r) for r in rows])\n\nsolutions = []\nfor w in range(2,10) (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "```python\nrows_str = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\nrows = [list(map(int, s)) for s in rows_str]\n\nsolutions = []\n# x from 2 to 9 inclusive (positive integer below 10, other than 1)\nfor x in range(2,10):\n    for y in range(3,11):  # smaller index of adjacent swap, not involving 0,1,2,12 => y in 3..10\n        for phase in [0,1]:  # phase 0: weight 1 at even indices; phase 1: weight x at even indices\n            ok = True\n            for r in rows:\n                # swap columns y and y+1\n                d = r[:]\n                d[y], d[y+1] = d[y+1], d[y]\n                s = 0\n                for i, digit in enumerate(d):\n                    w = 1 if (i % 2 == phase) else x\n                    s += digit * w\n                if s % 10 != 0:\n                    ok = False\n                    break\n            if ok:\n                solutions.append((x, y, phase))\nsolutions\n```", "expected": "7, 9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 1014, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 53.27, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 53.27, "prof_tok_in": 792, "prof_tok_out": 3701, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:18:35.552203", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "raw_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b7f857e4-d8aa-4387-af2a-0e844df5b9d8", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded variant:\n\n---\n\nYou need to answer the following question correctly.\n\n**Question:** A Python script is shown in the attached image. Execute this Python code using the array of strings provided below. The script will output a URL that points to C++ source code. Take that C++ code, compile it, and run it against the integer array [35, 12, 8, 99, 21, 5]. After sorting the result, compute the sum of the third and fifth integers in the sorted list.\n\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jk", "augmented_prompt": "## Patch history (memory)\nThese record what changed in earlier versions and why:\n- [2 @v279] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests, re, textwrap, sys, json, os\n\n# Reconstruct the URL from the array pieces (as deduced)\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jkl', 'tps', '/Q', 'pqr', 'stu', ':', '//', 'rose', 'vwx', 'yz1', '234', 'tta', '567', '890', 'cod', 'e.', 'or', 'g/', 'wiki', '/', 'ing', 'sort', 'abc' , 'or', 'it', 'hms', 'mno' , 'uic', 'ksort', '#', 'ht' ]\n\n# The Python script in the image likely filter (because prior task in this benchmark)\n- [2 @v170] [AVOID] ```python:  -> ```python\nimport requests, re, textwrap, sys, json, os\n\nurl = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort#C++\"\ntry:\n    r = requests.get(url, timeout=20)\n    print(\"status\", r.status_code)\n    # print a snippet around C++\n    text = r.text\n    idx = text.find(\"C++\")\n    print(text[idx-200:idx+500])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error\", e)\n``` (because prior task in this benchmark)", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>python_exec\n<tool_call:6124c78e>![python]\nimport requests, re, textwrap, sys, json, os\n\nurl = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort?action=raw\"\nr = requests.get(url, timeout=20)\nprint(\"status\", r.status_code)\ntext = r.text\n# Find the C++ section. In raw wikitext, sections are marked by =={{header|C++}}== or similar.\n# Let's locate it.\nm = re.search(r'==\\{\\{header\\|C\\+\\+\\}\\}==(.*?)(?=\\n==\\{\\{header\\|)', text, re.DOTALL)\nif m:\n    section = m.group(1)\n    print(\"Section length:\", len(section))\n    # Print first 2000 chars\n    print(section[:2000])\nelse:\n    # try other patterns\n    print(\"No match, searching for C++\")\n    idx = text.find(\"C++\")\n    print(text[idx-200:idx+800])\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "47", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 993, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 74.21, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 74.21, "prof_tok_in": 770, "prof_tok_out": 5201, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
