{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:46:40.557077", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_5cfb274c-0207-4aa7-9575-6ac0bd95d9b2", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Each cell in the attached spreadsheet represents a plot of land. The color of the cell indicates who owns that plot. Green cells are plots owned by Earl Smith. Can Earl walk through every plot he owns (and no other plots) and return to his starting plot without backtracking? For this question, consider backtracking to be any instance where Earl would enter a plot of land he had already entered since leaving his starting plot.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text⟩Each cell in the attached spreadsheet represents a plot of land Green cells are plots owned by Earl Smith Can Earl walk through every plot he owns</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "No", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 9.51, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 9.51, "prof_tok_in": 309, "prof_tok_out": 524, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:46:44.063906", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_544b7f0c-173a-4377-8d56-57b36eb26ddf", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In Valentina Re’s contribution to the 2017 book “World Building: Transmedia, Fans, Industries”, what horror movie does the author cite as having popularized metalepsis between a dream world and reality? Use the complete name with article if any.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "A Nightmare on Elm Street", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 12.38, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 12.38, "prof_tok_in": 278, "prof_tok_out": 117, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:01.860228", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_54612da3-fd56-4941-80f4-5eb82330de25", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached file shows the locomotives in the collection of a North American railroad museum. How many wheels do the listed steam locomotives have in total?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport os\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "60", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 24.3, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 24.3, "prof_tok_in": 252, "prof_tok_out": 500, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:05.653837", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, please report the longest word that comes first, alphabetically. Oh, and I know that there might be differen", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, bisect, time\n\nurl = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt'\nprint('Downloading dictionary...')\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwords = [w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip().isalpha()]\nword_set = set(words)\nwords_sorted = sorted(word_set)\nprint('Dictionary size:', len(word_set))\n\nboard = [list('abrl'),\n         list('eite'),\n         list('ions'),\n         list('fpei')]\n\ndef is_prefix(s):\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(words_sorted, s)\n    return idx < len(words_sorted) and words_sorted[idx].startswith(s)\n\nfound = set()\nmax_len = 0\n\ndef dfs(r, c, visited, cur):\n    global max_len\n    ch = board[r][c]\n    nxt = cur + ch\n    if not is_prefix(nxt):\n        return\n    if nxt in word_set and len(nxt) >= 3:\n        found.add(nxt)\n        if len(nxt) > max_len:\n            max_len = len(nxt)\n    visited.add((r,c))\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr==0 and dc==0: continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<4 and 0<=nc<4 and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                dfs(nr, nc, visited, nxt)\n    visited.remove((r,c))\n\nfor r in range(4):\n    for c in range(4):\n        dfs(r, c, set(), '')\n\nprint('Max length found:', max_len)\ncandidates = sorted([w for w in found if len(w)==max_len])\nprint('Number of candidates:', len(candidates))\nprint('First few candidates:', candidates[:10])\nprint('Answer:', candidates[0] if candidates else None)\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 51.22, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 51.22, "prof_tok_in": 362, "prof_tok_out": 2187, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
