{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:13.934490", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_65638e28-7f37-4fa7-b7b9-8c19bb609879", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The book with the doi 10.1353/book.24372 concerns a certain neurologist. According to chapter 2 of the book, what author influenced this neurologist’s belief in “endopsychic myths”? Give the last name only.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>query>10.1353/book.24372</query>\n<parameter name=\"query\">10.1353/book.24372</parameter>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Kleinpaul", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 3.8, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3.8, "prof_tok_in": 277, "prof_tok_out": 162, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:13.934559", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_50ad0280-0819-4bd9-b275-5de32d3b5bcb", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Pull out the sentence in the following 5x7 block of text. Read from left to right and use all of the letters in order:\n\nTHESE\nAGULL\nGLIDE\nDPEAC\nEFULL\nYTOMY\nCHAIR", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "THE SEAGULL GLIDED PEACEFULLY TO MY CHAIR", "expected": "The seagull glided peacefully to my chair.", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 46.68, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 46.68, "prof_tok_in": 277, "prof_tok_out": 2381, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:14.425798", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_9e1fc53b-46ff-49a1-9d05-9e6faac34cc5", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: A 5-man group made up of one tank, one healer, and three DPS is doing a dungeon that was just released in World of Warcraft. Two are plate wearers and two are cloth wearers. At the final boss, both the tank and the healer are casting holy spells. Ice and fire are being used, each one by a different DPS. A bear from the group is attacking the boss. Metamorphosis is cast. The Kilt of the Forgotten One drops as loot, but no one can use it. If all", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search_1\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Death Knight, Hunter, Paladin, Priest, Warlock", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 56.7, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 56.7, "prof_tok_in": 369, "prof_tok_out": 2097, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:14.837371", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-separated list of countries in alphabetical order. Use the countries most common names in english when answering.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "</think:6124c78e>I'll fetch the World Bank data via their API.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport requests, json, time\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\nyears = \"2001:2010\"\nbase = f\"http://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": years, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\n\nall_rows = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n    r = requests.get(base, params=params, timeout=30)\n    data = r.json()\n    if len(data) < 2 or not data[1]:\n        break\n    all_rows.extend(data[1])\n    total = data[0]['total']\n    if page * 1000 >= total:\n        break\n    page += 1\n    time.sleep(0.2)\n\nprint(\"rows:\", len(all_rows))\n# structure: each row has country, countryiso3code, date, value\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ndata_by_country = defaultdict(dict)\nfor row in all_rows:\n    c = row['country']['value']\n    iso = row['countryiso3code']\n    yr = int(row['date'])\n    val = row['value']\n    if val is not None:\n        data_by_country[(c,iso)][yr] = val\n\n# filter\nrequired_years = set(range(2001,2011))\nresult = []\nfor (c,iso), yv in data_by_country.items():\n    if required_years.issubset(set(yv.keys())):\n        if all(yv[y] > 35 for y in required_years):\n            result.append((c,iso))\n\nprint(\"count:\", len(result))\nfor x in sorted(result):\n    print(x)\n```", "expected": "Brunei, China, Morocco, Singapore", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 15.32, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 15.32, "prof_tok_in": 280, "prof_tok_out": 726, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
