{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:16.779010", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_65da0822-a48a-4a68-bbad-8ed1b835a834", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: All of the individuals who formally held the position of United States secretary of homeland security prior to April 2019, excluding those who held the position in an acting capacity, have a bachelor's degree. Of the universities that these bachelor's degrees were from, which is the westernmost university and which is the easternmost university? Give them to me as a comma-separated list, I only want the name of the cities where the universitie", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query_t__>Tom Ridge bachelor's degree university location</parameter>\n</invoke>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Santa Clara, Boston", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 62.55, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 62.55, "prof_tok_in": 321, "prof_tok_out": 1124, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:17.208564", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_17b5a6a3-bc87-42e8-b0fb-6ab0781ef2cc", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I’m researching species that became invasive after people who kept them as pets released them. There’s a certain species of fish that was popularized as a pet by being the main character of the movie Finding Nemo. According to the USGS, where was this fish found as a nonnative species, before the year 2020? I need the answer formatted as the five-digit zip codes of the places the species was found, separated by commas if there is more than one", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>USGS nonnative clownfish Amphiprion ocellaris zip code before 2020</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "34689", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 250.7, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 250.7, "prof_tok_in": 321, "prof_tok_out": 415, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:17.622559", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_076c8171-9b3b-49b9-a477-244d2a532826", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached file contains a list of vendors in the Liminal Springs mall, along with each vendor’s monthly revenue and the rent they pay the mall. I want you to find the vendor that makes the least money, relative to the rent it pays. Then, tell me what is listed in the “type” column for that vendor.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "</think:6124c78e>I'll start by exploring the environment to find the attached file.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os\nimport glob\n\n# List files in current directory and common locations\nprint(\"Current directory:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"\\nFiles in current directory:\")\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    print(f)\n\nprint(\"\\nSearching for common file types...\")\nfor ext in ['*.csv', '*.xlsx', '*.xls', '*.json', '*.txt', '*.tsv']:\n    found = glob.glob(ext)\n    if found:\n        print(ext, \"->\", found)\n```", "expected": "Finance", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 74.38, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 74.38, "prof_tok_in": 292, "prof_tok_out": 287, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:21.962065", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3da89939-209c-4086-8520-7eb734e6b4ef", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I was referencing each of the tables in the file from papers that were cited by the \"Trans fatty acid contents in chocolates and chocolate wafers in Turkey\" paper. I lost my own reference sheet and need to know which of the papers each table came from. The file may not use the full table caption. If the references in the\"Trans fatty acid\" paper bibliography were numbered starting with 1, give me the numbers in the order that they would be used", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>query>Trans fatty acid contents in chocolates and chocolate wafers in Turkey</query>\n<summary>Search for the paper and its references/Excel file</summary>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "8, 29, 22, 1, 8, 26", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 19.19, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 19.19, "prof_tok_in": 337, "prof_tok_out": 361, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:21.962248", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4fc2f1ae-8625-45b5-ab34-ad4433bc21f8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Who nominated the only Featured Article on English Wikipedia about a dinosaur that was promoted in November 2016?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "FunkMonk", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 10.11, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 10.11, "prof_tok_in": 246, "prof_tok_out": 84, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:47:21.962315", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0bdb7c40-671d-4ad1-9ce3-986b159c0ddc", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In NASA's Astronomy Picture of the Day on 2006 January 21, two astronauts are visible, with one appearing much smaller than the other. As of August 2023, out of the astronauts in the NASA Astronaut Group that the smaller astronaut was a member of, which one spent the least time in space, and how many minutes did he spend in space, rounded to the nearest minute? Exclude any astronauts who did not spend any time in space. Give the last name of t", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text|>NASA Astronomy Picture of the Day 2006 January 21 two astronauts smaller</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "White; 5876", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 306.02, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 306.02, "prof_tok_in": 337, "prof_tok_out": 291, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
