{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:49:19.308276", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_56db2318-640f-477a-a82f-bc93ad13e882", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The following numbers function similarly to ISBN 13 numbers, however, their validation methods are slightly different. Rather than using alternate weights of 1 and 3, the checksum digit is calculated with an alternate weight of 1 and some other positive integer less than 10. Otherwise, the checksum digit is calculated as expected. Unfortunately, there is an error in the data. Two adjacent columns have been transposed. These errored columns do ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nnumbers = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\n\nsolutions = []\nfor w in range(2, 10):\n    for y in range(3, 11):  # smaller index of adjacent pair, not involving 0,1,2,12\n        ok = True\n        for row in numbers:\n            digits = [int(ch) for ch in row]\n            O = sum((1 if i % 2 == 0 else w) * digits[i] for i in range(13))\n            if y % 2 == 0:\n                D = digits[y+1] - digits[y]\n            else:\n                D = digits[y] - digits[y+1]\n            if (O % 10) != ((w - 1) * D % 10):\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if ok:\n            solutions.append((w, y))\nsolutions\n```", "expected": "7, 9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 31.22, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 31.22, "prof_tok_in": 469, "prof_tok_out": 5520, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
