{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:53:09.667454", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_04a04a9b-226c-43fd-b319-d5e89743676f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If we assume all articles published by Nature in 2020 (articles, only, not book reviews/columns, etc) relied on statistical significance to justify their findings and they on average came to a p-value of 0.04, how many papers would be incorrect as to their claims of statistical significance? Round the value up to the next integer.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "41", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 744.37, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 744.37, "prof_tok_in": 295, "prof_tok_out": 1299, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:53:09.667519", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_8d46b8d6-b38a-47ff-ac74-cda14cf2d19b", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: What percentage of the total penguin population according to the upper estimates on english Wikipedia at the end of 2012 is made up by the penguins in this file that don't live on Dream Island or have beaks longer than 42mm? Round to the nearest five decimal places.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "</think:6124c78e>I'll start by exploring the environment to find the referenced file and then search for the Wikipedia population estimate.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os, sys, glob\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\nprint('---')\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.startswith('.'):\n            print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "0.00033", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 744.37, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 744.37, "prof_tok_in": 280, "prof_tok_out": 425, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:53:09.667577", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_9318445f-fe6a-4e1b-acbf-c68228c9906a", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: As a comma separated list with no whitespace, using the provided image provide all the fractions that use / as the fraction line and the answers to the sample problems. Order the list by the order in which the fractions appear.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll search for this specific question to identify the image and context.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>raw⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>q⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>>\nAs a comma separated list with no whitespace, using the provided image provide all the fractions that use / as the fraction line and the answers to the sample problems\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "3/4,1/4,3/4,3/4,2/4,1/2,5/35,7/21,30/5,30/5,3/4,1/15,1/3,4/9,1/8,32/23,103/170", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 744.37, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 744.37, "prof_tok_in": 536, "prof_tok_out": 989, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:53:09.667639", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_1f975693-876d-457b-a649-393859e79bf3", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Hi, I was out sick from my classes on Friday, so I'm trying to figure out what I need to study for my Calculus mid-term next week. My friend from class sent me an audio recording of Professor Willowbrook giving out the recommended reading for the test, but my headphones are broken :(\n\nCould you please listen to the recording for me and tell me the page numbers I'm supposed to go over? I've attached a file called Homework.mp3 that has the recor", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll help you extract the page numbers from the audio recording. Let me first access the file and analyze it.\n\nTool call list:\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `import os\nimport glob\n\n# List files in current directory and common locations\nprint(\"Current directory:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"\\nFiles in current directory:\")\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    print(f\"  {f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nSearching for Homework.mp3:\")\nfor path in glob.glob('**/Homework.mp3', recursive=True):\n    print(f\"  Found: {path}\")\n    print(f\"  Size: {os.path.getsize(path)} bytes\")`\n\n1. Tool: `read_file`\n   - `path` = `Homework.mp3`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `import sys\nprint(sys.version)\ntry:\n    import speech_recognition as sr\n    print(\"speech_recognition available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"speech_recognition not available:\", e)\ntry:\n    import whisper\n    print(\"whisper available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"whisper not available:\", e)\ntry:\n    import torch\n    print(\"torch available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"torch not available:\", e)\ntry:\n    import librosa\n    print(\"librosa available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"librosa not available:\", e)\ntry:\n    import pydub\n    print(\"pydub available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"pydub not available:\", e)\ntry:\n    import soundfile\n    print(\"soundfile available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"soundfile not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `web_search`\n   - `query` = `Professor Willowbrook Calculus mid-term recommended reading page numbers Homework.mp3`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `import os, glob\nfor path in glob.glob('**/*', recursive=True):\n    if os.path.isfile(path):\n        print(path, os.path.getsize(path))`", "expected": "132, 133, 134, 197, 245", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 744.37, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 744.37, "prof_tok_in": 688, "prof_tok_out": 9773, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
