{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:55:51.519050", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_5a0c1adf-205e-4841-a666-7c3ef95def9d", "task_desc": "Answer the question below precisely.\n\nQuestion: Among the Malko Competition winners from the 20th Century (post-1977), there is exactly one whose recorded nationality belongs to a country that has since ceased to exist. What is that recipient's first name?", "augmented_prompt": "## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: What is the first name of the only Malko Competition recipient from the 20th Century (after 1977) whose nationality on record is a country that no lon\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Malko Competition winners list nationality</tex\nAvoid: The specific pitfall to avoid is executing a single search query without preliminary disambiguation (e.g., first query for 'Malko Competition' to get the list then filter for natio", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Malko Competition winners list nationality</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Claus", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 627, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 259.66, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 259.66, "prof_tok_in": 399, "prof_tok_out": 206, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:55:51.519127", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_2dfc4c37-fec1-4518-84a7-10095d30ad75", "task_desc": "The following question needs an accurate answer:\n\nQuestion: Looking at Box Office Mojo's 2020 Worldwide Box Office rankings, what number of films appearing in the top 10 highest-grossing worldwide movies also appear in the top 10 highest-grossing domestic movies? Provide your answer as a numerical integer value.", "augmented_prompt": "## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: According to Box Office Mojo's 2020 Worldwide Box Office list, how many of the top 10 highest-grossing worldwide movies are also on the top 10 highest\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Box Office Mojo 2020 world\nAvoid: Specific pitfall to avoid is proceeding with a single search for one list type without enumerating and executing queries for all required data sources first; concrete indicator is ", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Box Office Mojo 2020 worldwide box office top 10 highest grossing movies list", "expected": "6", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 627, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 165.93, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 165.93, "prof_tok_in": 404, "prof_tok_out": 122, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:55:51.519209", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_08f3a05f-5947-4089-a4c4-d4bcfaa6b7a0", "task_desc": "Reword the following question precisely, keeping all facts, numbers, entities, constraints, and the expected answer unchanged:\n\n---\n\nLet $x_0 = -5$ and $f(x) = x^3 + 4x^2 - 3x + 8$. Apply Newton's Method, and after each step round to four decimal places. Determine the smallest integer $n$ for which the iteration satisfies $n = n + 1$.", "augmented_prompt": "## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: Given $x_0 = -5$ and $f(x) = x^3 + 4x^2 - 3x + 8$, what is the smallest $n$ where using Newton's Method $n = n+1$ after rounding to four decimal place\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Newt\nAvoid: Correct approach but 0 missing steps", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code_execution<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>code>import decimal\nfrom decimal import Decimal, getcontext\n\n# Set high precision\ngetcontext().prec = 50\ngetcontext().rounding = decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP\n\ndef f(x):\n    return x**3 + Decimal('4')*x**2 - Decimal('3')*x + Decimal('8')\n\ndef fp(x):\n    return Decimal('3')*x**2 + Decimal('8')*x - Decimal('3')\n\ndef round4(x):\n    return x.quantize(Decimal('0.0001'), rounding=decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)\n\nx = Decimal('-5')\niterates = [x]\nfor i in range(1, 20):\n    fx = f(x)\n    fpx = fp(x)\n    if fpx == 0:\n        print(\"zero derivative\")\n        break\n    x_next = x - fx/fpx\n    x_next_rounded = round4(x_next)\n    iterates.append(x_next_rounded)\n    if x_next_rounded == x:\n        print(f\"Converged at step i={i}, x_{i-1}={x}, x_{i}={x_next_rounded}\")\n        break\n    x = x_next_rounded\n\nprint(\"Iterates:\")\nfor idx, val in enumerate(iterates):\n    print(idx, val)\nprint(\"Smallest n such that x_n == x_{n+1}? n =\", len(iterates)-2)\n</code>\n</parameter>\n</invoke>\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Run code to compute Newton iterates with rounding to 4 decimals.", "expected": "2", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 483, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 171.82, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 171.82, "prof_tok_in": 424, "prof_tok_out": 1568, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:55:51.519292", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4d51c4bf-4b0e-4f3d-897b-3f6687a7d9f2", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nPlease answer the following question with precision.\n\nQuestion: A retractable awning company maintains a client list in this spreadsheet. Every client has placed an order for a new backyard awning in the past 90 days. The company produces two distinct designs: one tailored to block sunrises and another tailored to block sunsets. In this region, homes with odd-numbered street addresses face east, while homes with even-numbered street addresses face west. Among t", "augmented_prompt": "## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: This spreadsheet contains a list of clients for a retractable awning company. Each client has ordered a new awning for the back of their house within \nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩retractable awning company spreadsheet clients odd-numbered street addr\nAvoid: Always complete full query strings prior to tool invocation and validate by running with incrementally shorter versions; concrete indicator is seeing zero results when all key term", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\"retractable awning\" \"spreadsheet\" \"clients\" \"street address\"\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "8", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 627, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "