{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:58:30.915408", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0b260a57-3f3a-4405-9f29-6d7a1012dbfb", "task_desc": "Here is the reworded task:\n\n---\n\nDetermine the answer to the following question with precision.\n\nQuestion: As of 2022, when examining ScienceDirect data, calculate the sample standard deviation of the count of Reference Works for each Life Science domain and for Health Sciences — then compute the difference between these two standard deviations, rounded to 3 decimal places.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: On ScienceDirect, what is the difference to 3 decimal places in the sample standard deviations of the number of Reference Works in each Life Science d\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  <argument name=\"query\">ScienceDirect number of Reference Works Life Science domain Health Sciences 2022</argument>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\nLesson: The web search strategy failed because the specific mechanism of relying on a general keyword query did not access ScienceDirect's hierarchical category pages for Life Science doma", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<argument name=\"query\">ScienceDirect 2022 Reference Works Life Science domain Health Sciences count</argument>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "0.269", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 680, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_