{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:58:30.915854", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_17b5a6a3-bc87-42e8-b0fb-6ab0781ef2cc", "task_desc": "I'm conducting research on invasive species that originated from pet releases. One particular fish species gained widespread popularity as a pet after starring as the protagonist in the animated film *Finding Nemo*. Per USGS records, in which locations was this fish documented as a nonnative species prior to 2020? Please provide the answer as five-digit ZIP codes, separated by commas if multiple locations exist.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: I’m researching species that became invasive after people who kept them as pets released them. There’s a certain species of fish that was popularized \nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>USGS nonnative clownfish Amphiprion ocellaris zip code before 2020</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>USGS Nonindigenous Aquatic Species Amphiprion ocellaris nonnative zip code</arg_value:6124c78e>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "34689", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 507, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 238.35, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 238.35, "prof_tok_in": 394, "prof_tok_