{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:58:30.916169", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_983bba7c-c092-455f-b6c9-7857003d48fc", "task_desc": "**Reworded Task (Variant 1):**\n\nPlease provide an accurate response to the following query.\n\nQuery: Across the papers authored by Ilias Lagkouvardos and Olga Tapia concerning the alvei species belonging to the genus whose name references Copenhagen, which animals appear in both of their works (excluding their bibliographies) that are likewise found in the 2021 multicenter, randomized, double-blind study referenced on the alvei species' Wikipedia entry?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: What animals that were mentioned in both Ilias Lagkouvardos's and Olga Tapia's papers on the alvei species of the genus named for Copenhagen outside t\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n  -query\tHafnia alvei Wikipedia 2021 multicenter randomized double-blind study\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n  -query\tHafnia alvei Wikipedia 2021 multicenter randomized double-blind study\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "mice", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 454, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 239.76, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 239.76, "prof_tok_in": 414, "prof_tok_out": 523, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:58:30.916276", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Please answer the following question with precision.\n\nQuestion: Per World Bank data, during each individual year from 2001 through 2010, which countries maintained gross savings exceeding 35% of their GDP? Return your response as an alphabetically sorted, comma-separated list of countries, using their most common English names.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-\nAs recorded: </think:6124c78e>I'll fetch the World Bank data via their API.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport requests, json, time\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\nyears = \"2001:2010\"\nbase = f\"http://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": years, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\n\nall_rows = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n    r = requests.get(base,", "response": "```python\nimport requests, json, time, sys\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\ndate = \"2001:2010\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": date, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\n\nall_data = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params, timeout=30)\n    if r.status_code != 200:\n        print(\"Error\", r.status_code)\n        break\n    j = r.json()\n    if len(j) < 2 or not j[1]:\n        break\n    all_data.extend(j[1])\n    total = j[0]['total']\n    if len(all_data) >= total:\n        break\n    page += 1\n    time.sleep(0.2)\n\nprint(\"records\", len(all_data))\n# Structure: each record: country, date, value\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n# store by country iso2 and name\ncountry_vals = defaultdict(dict)  # iso2 -> {year: value}\ncountry_name = {}\nfor rec in all_data:\n    iso = rec['countryiso3code']  # maybe empty for aggregates? use country.id\n    cid = rec['country']['id']\n    cname = rec['country']['value']\n    year = int(rec['date'])\n    val = rec['value']\n    country_vals[cid].setdefault('name', cname)\n    if val is not None:\n        country_vals[cid][year] = val\n\n# Filter: only countries (not aggregates). World Bank country id for aggregates are like 'WLD','HIC','LIC','MIC','LMC','UMC','EAS','ECS','LCN','MEA','NAC','SAS','SSF','ARB','CEB','EUU','OED','PSS','PST','PRE','LDC','HPC','IBD','IBT','IDA','IDB','IDX','LIC','MIC','LMY','EMU','FCS','HIC','LIC','MIC','OSS','SST','TEA','TEC','TLA','TMN','TSA','TSS','TWN'? Actually Taiwan not included. We need to exclude if countryiso3code is empty? Let's inspect.\n# We'll just check if cid is 3-letter iso? Most countries have 3-letter iso. Aggregates also have 3-letter codes like 'WLD','HIC','LIC','MIC','LMY','OED','ARB','EUU','EMU','FCS','LDC','PSS','PST','PRE','CEB','IBD','IBT','IDA','IDB','IDX','OSS','SST','TEA','TEC','TLA','TMN','TSA','TSS','TWN'? Wait TWN is Taiwan (not official but included maybe). But we can filter by checking if cid in list of aggregate codes. Better: World Bank API has endpoint for countries only: /v2/country?format=json. We can fetch list of country ids that are 'country' (not 'aggregate').\n```\n\nLet's fetch country list to distinguish.</think:6124c78e>```python\n# Fetch list of countries and aggregates\nc_url = \"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country\"\nc_params = {\"format\":\"json\",\"per_page\":1000}\nr = requests.get(c_url, params=c_params, timeout=30)\ncj = r.json()\ncountries = {}\nfor item in cj[1]:\n    countries[item['id']] = item['name']\n    # item['region']['value'] maybe 'Aggregates' for aggregates? Actually aggregates have region 'Aggregates'?\n    # Let's print a few aggregates\nprint(\"total countries\", len(countries))\n# Show some with region Aggregates\nagg = [ (item['id'], item['name'], item['region']['value']) for item in cj[1] if item['region']['value'] == 'Aggregates']\nprint(\"aggregates count\", len(agg))\nprint(agg[:20])\n```\n\nLet's run.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport requests, time\nc_url = \"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country\"\nc_params = {\"format\":\"json\",\"per_page\":1000}\nr = requests.get(c_url, params=c_params, timeout=30)\ncj = r.json()\nitems = cj[1]\nprint(\"total\", len(items))\nagg = [ (it['id'], it['name']) for it in items if it['region']['value'] == 'Aggregates' ]\nprint(\"agg count\", len(agg))\nfor x in agg: print(x)\n```\n\nNow we need to combine. Let's run full script.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport requests, time\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# 1. Get country list to know which ids are aggregates\nc_url = \"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country\"\nr = requests.get(c_url, params={\"format\":\"json\",\"per_page\":1000}, timeout=30)\ncj = r.json()\naggregate_ids = set()\ncountry_names = {}\nfor it in cj[1]:\n    if it['region']['value'] == 'Aggregates':\n        aggregate_ids.add(it['id'])\n    else:\n        country_names[it['id']] = it['name']\n\n# 2. Get indicator data\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\ndate = \"2001:2010\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": date, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\nall_data = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params, timeout=30)\n    j = r.json()\n    if len(j) < 2 or not j[1]:\n        break\n    all_data.extend(j[1])\n    total = j[0]['total']\n    if len(all_data) >= total:\n        break\n    page += 1\n    time.sleep(0.1)\n\nprint(\"records\", len(all_data))\n\n# 3. Organize\nby_country = defaultdict(dict)\nfor rec in all_data:\n    cid = rec['country']['id']\n    year = int(rec['date'])\n    val = rec['value']\n    if val is not None:\n        by_country[cid][year] = val\n\n# 4. Filter\nyears_needed = list(range(2001,2011))\nqualifying = []\nfor cid, yvals in by_country.items():\n    if cid in aggregate_ids:\n        continue\n    if all(yvals.get(y) is not None and yvals.get(y) > 35 for y in years_needed):\n        qualifying.append((cid, country_names.get(cid, cid)))\n\nprint(\"Qualifying count:\", len(qualifying))\nfor q in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x: x[1]):\n    print(q)\n```\n\nLet's run this.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport requests, time\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nc_url = \"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country\"\nr = requests.get(c_url, params={\"format\":\"json\",\"per_page\":1000}, timeout=30)\ncj = r.json()\naggregate_ids = set()\ncountry_names = {}\nfor it in cj[1]:\n    if it['region']['value'] == 'Aggregates':\n        aggregate_ids.add(it['id'])\n    else:\n        country_names[it['id']] = it['name']\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\ndate = \"2001:2010\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": date, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\nall_data = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params, timeout=30)\n    j = r.json()\n    if len(j) < 2 or not j[1]:\n        break\n    all_data.extend(j[1])\n    total = j[0]['total']\n    if len(all_data) >= total:\n        break\n    page += 1\n    time.sleep(0.1)\n\nprint(\"records\", len(all_data))\nby_country = defaultdict(dict)\nfor rec in all_data:\n    cid = rec['country']['id']\n    year = int(rec['date'])\n    val = rec['value']\n    if val is not None:\n        by_country[cid][year] = val\n\nyears_needed = list(range(2001,2011))\nqualifying = []\nfor cid, yvals in by_country.items():\n    if cid in aggregate_ids:\n        continue\n    ok = True\n    for y in years_needed:\n        v = yvals.get(y)\n        if v is None or v <= 35:\n            ok = False\n            break\n    if ok:\n        qualifying.append((cid, country_names.get(cid, cid)))\n\nprint(\"count\", len(qualifying))\nfor q in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x: x[1]):\n    print(q)\n```\n\nWe need to see output. Let's execute.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport requests, time\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nc_url = \"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country\"\nr = requests.get(c_url, params={\"format\":\"json\",\"per_page\":1000}, timeout=30)\ncj = r.json()\naggregate_ids = set()\ncountry_names = {}\nfor it in cj[1]:\n    if it['region']['value'] == 'Aggregates':\n        aggregate_ids.add(it['id'])\n    else:\n        country_names[it['id']] = it['name']\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\ndate = \"2001:2010\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": date, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\nall_data = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n    r = requests.get(url, params=params, timeout=30)\n    j = r.json()\n    if len(j) < 2 or not j[1]:\n        break\n    all_data.extend(j[1])\n    total = j[0]['total']\n    if len(all_data) >= total:\n        break\n    page += 1\n    time.sleep(0.1)\n\nprint(\"records\", len(all_data))\nby_country = defaultdict(dict)\nfor rec in all_data:\n    cid = rec['country']['id']\n    year = int(rec['date'])\n    val = rec['value']\n    if val is not None:\n        by_country[cid][year] = val\n\nyears_needed = list(range(2001,2011))\nqualifying = []\nfor cid, yvals in by_country.items():\n    if cid in aggregate_ids:\n        continue\n    ok = True\n    for y in years_needed:\n        v = yvals.get(y)\n        if v is None or v <= 35:\n            ok = False\n            break\n    if ok:\n        qualifying.append((cid, country_names.get(cid, cid)))\n\nprint(\"count\", len(qualifying))\nfor q in sorted(qualifying, key=lambda x: x[1]):\n    print(q)\n```\n\nLet's see results. I'll simulate? Actually I need to run cod