{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:58:30.916822", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_ad37a656-079a-49f9-a493-7b739c9167d1", "task_desc": "On July 15, 2008, the website Phys.org ran a story concerning a disaster. Determine the explosive yield of that disaster as reported by Encyclopedia Britannica, and then identify the United States nuclear test that matched that same yield. Your response must consist solely of the final word in the test's name.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: On July 15, 2008, Phys.org published an article about a catastrophe. Find the explosive force of this catastrophe according to Encyclopedia Britannica\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\t\n```json\n{\"query\":\"Phys.org July 15 2008 catastrophe article explosive force Encyclopedia Britannica\"}\n```</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n```json\n{\"query\":\"Phys.org July 15 2008 catastrophe disaster article\"}\n```</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Bravo", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 480, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 243.58, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 243.58, "prof_tok_in": 377, "prof_tok_out": 168, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T16:58:30.916943", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_076c8171-9b3b-49b9-a477-244d2a532826", "task_desc": "The attached file lists vendors at the Liminal Springs mall, showing each vendor's monthly revenue and rent. Identify the vendor with the lowest revenue-to-rent ratio. Then, report the value in the \"type\" column for that vendor.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: The attached file contains a list of vendors in the Liminal Springs mall, along with each vendor’s monthly revenue and the rent they pay the mall. I w\nAs recorded: </think:6124c78e>I'll start by exploring the environment to find the attached file.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os\nimport glob\n\n# List files in current directory and common locations\nprint(\"Current directory:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"\\nFiles in current directory:\")\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    print(f)\n\nprint(\"\\nSearching for common file types...\")\nfor ext in ['*.csv', '*.xlsx', '*.xls', '*.jso", "response": "```python\nimport os, glob\n\nprint(\"cwd:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"listdir:\")\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    print(f)\n\nprint(\"\\nSearch recursively for files (max depth 3):\")\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    depth = root.count(os.sep) - os.getcwd().count(os.sep)\n    if depth <= 3:\n        for f in files:\n            print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "Finance", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 677, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 237.94, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 237.94, "prof_tok_in": 430, "prof_tok_out": 256, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
