{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:01:59.384024", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_872bfbb1-9ccf-49f6-8c5f-aa22818ccd66", "task_desc": "Answer the question below with precision.\n\nQuestion: In the 2008 artwork titled \"Embroidery from Uzbekistan,\" several fruits are depicted. Among those fruits, which ones also appeared on the breakfast menu from October 1949 aboard the ocean liner that subsequently served as a floating set piece for the movie \"The Last Voyage\"? Provide your answer as a comma-separated list, arranged in clockwise sequence according to their positions in the painting, beginning at the 12 o'clock mark. Use the plura", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: Which of the fruits shown in the 2008 painting \"Embroidery from Uzbekistan\" were served as part of the October 1949 breakfast menu for the ocean liner\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>query>Embroidery from Uzbekistan 2008 painting fruits</query>\n<name>search_painting</name>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>query>The Last Voyage film floating prop ocean liner</query>\n<name>search_film</name>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query\">Embroidery from Uzbekistan\" 2008 painting fruits</query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query\">Embroidery from Uzbekistan\" artwork</query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query\">The Last Voyage\" floating set piece ocean liner</query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "pears, bananas", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 677, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 339.34, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 339.34, "prof_tok_in": 467, "prof_tok_out": 338, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:01:59.384165", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_2d83110e-a098-4ebb-9987-066c06fa42d0", "task_desc": "The question appears to be written in reverse. Let me decode it:\n\nOriginal: \".rewsna eht sa 'tfel' drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\"\n\nReversed: \"If you understand this sentence, write the opposite of the word 'left' as the answer.\"\n\n---\n\nHere is the reworded version (variant 2):\n\n**Task:** Provide an accurate answer to the following question.\n\n**Question:** Assuming you can comprehend this sentence, output the antonym of the word \"left\" as your response.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 100%]\nTask: If you understand this sentence, write the opposite of the word \"left\" as the answer.\nAs recorded: </think:6124c78e>right", "response": "right", "expected": "Right", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 235, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 276.02, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 276.02, "prof_tok_in": 404, "prof_tok_out": 779, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:01:59.384324", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_9b54f9d9-35ee-4a14-b62f-d130ea00317f", "task_desc": "Among the text elements listed under CATEGORIES in the XML, which one holds the single food from the spreadsheet that never appears again under any alternative name?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: Which of the text elements under CATEGORIES in the XML would contain the one food in the spreadsheet that does not appear a second time under a differ\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text⟩\"does not appear a second time under a different name\" \"CATEGORIES\" XML\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text⟩\"does not appear a second time under a different name\" \"CATEGORIES\" XML\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Soups and Stews", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 498, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 339.34, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 339.34, "prof_tok_in": 354, "prof_tok_out": 363, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
