{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:06:16.846544", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b2c257e0-3ad7-4f05-b8e3-d9da973be36e", "task_desc": "Answer the following question precisely.\n\nQuestion: Assume this entire pint consists of ice cream. Based on the US federal standards for butterfat content as documented by Wikipedia in 2020, by what percentage does it exceed or fall short of those standards? Provide your answer as + or - followed by a number rounded to one decimal place.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: If this whole pint is made up of ice cream, how many percent above or below the US federal standards for butterfat content is it when using the standa\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩If this whole pint is made up of ice cream, how many percent above or below the US federal standards for butterfat content is it when using the standards as reported by Wikipedia in 2020</think:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\"Assume this entire pint consists of ice cream\" \"US federal standards for butterfat\" Wikipedia 2020</think:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "+4.6", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 581, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 276.01, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 276.01, "prof_tok_in": 404, "prof_tok_out": 319, "prof_ll