{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:06:16.846993", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_389793a7-ca17-4e82-81cb-2b3a2391b4b9", "task_desc": "You are a telecommunications engineer planning to erect cell phone towers along a highway. The reference file contains a diagram of the highway and adjacent houses. Each dash (\"-\") represents a mile marker. Each uppercase \"H\" denotes a house situated beside a mile marker, positioned either above or below the highway. A single cell phone tower can serve houses located along the highway within a 4-mile radius. Determine the smallest number of cell phone towers required to provide coverage to all h", "augmented_prompt": "## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: You are a telecommunications engineer who wants to build cell phone towers on a stretch of road. In the reference file is a layout of the road and nea\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): ```python\nimport os\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\n```\nAvoid: Taking environment inspection steps like os.listdir('.') to access the reference file instead of directly writing code to parse the layout and compute tower placements; concrete in", "response": "```python\nimport os, glob\n\n# Try common filenames\ncandidates = ['reference.txt', 'reference', 'diagram.txt', 'input.txt', 'layout.txt', 'highway.txt', 'houses.txt']\nfound = []\nfor c in candidates:\n    if os.path.exists(c):\n        found.append(c)\nprint(\"Found candidates:\", found)\n\n# If none, list all files (excluding this script)\nif not found:\n    for f in os.listdir('.'):\n        if os.path.isfile(f):\n            print(f)\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also search for any text-like files\nfor f in glob.glob('*'):\n    if os.path.isfile(f):\n        print(f)\n```\n\n```python\n# Try reading reference.txt if exists\nif os.path.exists('reference.txt'):\n    with open('reference.txt') as fh:\n        data = fh.read()\n    print(data[:2000])\nelse:\n    print(\"no reference.txt\")\n```", "expected": "3", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 523, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 392.27, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 392.27, "prof_tok_in": 431, "prof_tok_out": 1733, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
