{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:06:16.847349", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "I've been asked to reword the task, so here is the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nUsing the Boggle board below, determine the longest possible English word that can be formed:\n\n```\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n```\n\nStandard Boggle rules apply: words are built by connecting adjacent letters (horizontally, vertically, or diagonally), and each letter tile may be used at most once per word.\n\nAs the word list for this puzzle, use the `words_alpha` dictionary hosted at https://github.com/dwyl/english-words.\n\nIf multi", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can b\nAs recorded: ```python\nimport urllib.request, bisect, time\n\nurl = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt'\nprint('Downloading dictionary...')\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwords = [w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip().isalpha()]\nword_set = set(words)\nwords_sorted = sorted(word_set)\nprint('Dictionary size:', len(word_set))\n\nbo", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request\n\nurl = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt'\nprint('Downloading dictionary...')\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nword_set = set(w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip().isalpha())\nprint('Dict size:', len(word_set))\n\n# Build prefix set\nprefix_set = set()\nfor w in word_set:\n    for i in range(1, len(w)+1):\n        prefix_set.add(w[:i])\nprint('Prefix size:', len(prefix_set))\n\nboard = [\n    ['a','b','r','l'],\n    ['e','i','t','e'],\n    ['i','o','n','s'],\n    ['f','p','e','i']\n]\nrows = 4\ncols = 4\n\nbest_words = set()\nmax_len = 0\n\ndef dfs(r, c, visited, path):\n    global max_len\n    # prune if path not a prefix\n    if path not in prefix_set:\n        return\n    # if word, record\n    if path in word_set and len(path) >= 3:\n        if len(path) > max_len:\n            max_len = len(path)\n            best_words.clear()\n            best_words.add(path)\n        elif len(path) == max_len:\n            best_words.add(path)\n    # explore neighbors\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                visited.add((nr,nc))\n                dfs(nr, nc, visited, path + board[nr][nc])\n                visited.remove((nr,nc))\n\nfor r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n        visited = {(r,c)}\n        dfs(r, c, visited, board[r][c])\n\nprint('Max length:', max_len)\nprint('Best words count:', len(best_words))\nif best_words:\n    print('Alphabetically first:', sorted(best_words)[0])\n    print('All best:', sorted(best_words))\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 677, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 525.92, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 525.92, "prof_tok_in": 532, "prof_tok_out": 1879, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:06:16.847483", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3cef3a44-215e-4aed-8e3b-b1e3f08063b7", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded variant:\n\n---\n\nRespond accurately to the question below.\n\nQuestion: I'm putting together a grocery list for my mom, who teaches botany and is extremely particular about classification. I need to sort various foods under the correct headings on the list — if I place something in the wrong category, she'll refuse to purchase anything listed under that heading. Here's what I have so far:\n\nmilk, eggs, flour, whole bean coffee, Oreos, sweet potatoes, fresh basil, plums, green bean", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add di\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query_text⟩botanical fruit green beans corn bell pepper zucchini allspice acorns peanuts</query_text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query_text⟩botanical classification sweet potato basil broccoli celery lettuce vegetable not fruit green beans corn bell pepper zucchini fruit</query_text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 523, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "s