{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:06:16.909369", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_114d5fd0-e2ae-4b6d-a65a-870da2d19c08", "task_desc": "What day of the month in November was the Wikipedia article accessed, according to the endnote located in the penultimate paragraph of page 11 in the book identified by DOI 10.2307/j.ctv9b2xdv? Provide only the numerical day.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: In the endnote found in the second-to-last paragraph of page 11 of the book with the doi 10.2307/j.ctv9b2xdv, what date in November was the Wikipedia \nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text|>10.2307/j.ctv9b2xdv</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text|>10.2307/j.ctv9b2xdv</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "4", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 494, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 276.01, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 276.01, "prof_tok_in": 388, "prof_tok_out": 173, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:10:48.033969", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_56db2318-640f-477a-a82f-bc93ad13e882", "task_desc": "The following numbers operate like ISBN-13 codes but with a modified validation scheme. Instead of alternating weights of 1 and 3, the checksum digit is computed using alternating weights of 1 and some other positive integer below 10. Apart from that, the checksum calculation follows the standard procedure. Regrettably, the data contains a mistake: two neighboring columns have been swapped. The swapped columns are not the last column and do not include any of the first three columns. With this i", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: The following numbers function similarly to ISBN 13 numbers, however, their validation methods are slightly different. Rather than using alternate wei\nAs recorded: ```python\nnumbers = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\n\nsolutions = []\nfor w in range(2, 10):\n    for y in range(3, 11):  # smaller index of adjacent pair, not involving 0,1,2,12\n        ok = True\n        for row in number", "response": "```python\nnumbers = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\n\nsolutions = []\nfor x in range(2, 10):\n    for y in range(3, 11):  # smaller index of adjacent pair, not involving 0,1,2,12\n        ok = True\n        for row in numbers:\n            digits = list(map(int, row))\n            # swap columns y and y+1 to recover original\n            digits[y], digits[y+1] = digits[y+1], digits[y]\n            s = 0\n            for i, d in enumerate(digits):\n                w = 1 if i % 2 == 0 else x\n                s += w * d\n            if s % 10 != 0:\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if ok:\n            solutions.append((x, y))\nsolutions\n```", "expected": "7, 9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 677, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 778.3, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 778.3, "prof_tok_in": 659, "prof_tok_out": 1804, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:10:48.034815", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_32102e3e-d12a-4209-9163-7b3a104efe5d", "task_desc": "Answer the question below precisely.\n\nQuestion: The enclosed spreadsheet contains the inventory records of a Seattle, Washington-based movie and video game rental business. Among the Blu-Ray entries in this spreadsheet, which title is the oldest? Provide the title exactly as it appears in the spreadsheet.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 100%]\nTask: The attached spreadsheet shows the inventory for a movie and video game rental store in Seattle, Washington. What is the title of the oldest Blu-Ray r\nAs recorded: I need to find the specific spreadsheet mentioned. Let me search for it.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\ninventory movie video game rental store Seattle Washington Blu-Ray spreadsheet oldest\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search}\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query⟩\n\"Seattle\" \"movie and video game rental\" \"Blu-Ray\" \"spreadsheet\" \"inventory\"\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Time-Parking 2: Parallel Universe", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 577, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 332.59, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 332.59, "prof_tok_in": 380, "prof_tok_out": 423, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
