{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:10:48.123055", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_8d46b8d6-b38a-47ff-ac74-cda14cf2d19b", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nBased on the upper population estimates from the English Wikipedia at the close of 2012, what fraction of all penguins worldwide is represented by the penguins in this file that either do not reside on Dream Island or possess beaks exceeding 42mm in length? Provide your answer as a percentage rounded to five decimal places.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: What percentage of the total penguin population according to the upper estimates on english Wikipedia at the end of 2012 is made up by the penguins in\nAs recorded: </think:6124c78e>I'll start by exploring the environment to find the referenced file and then search for the Wikipedia population estimate.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os, sys, glob\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\nprint('---')\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.startswith('.'):\n            print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "response": "```python\nimport os\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.startswith('.'):\n            print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "0.00033", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 636, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 332.59, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 332.59, "prof_tok_in": 436, "prof