{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:10:48.123635", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7a4a336d-dcfa-45a0-b014-824c7619e8de", "task_desc": "Answer the question below with precision.\n\nQuestion: In the YouTube video posted by \"GameGrumps\" on May 14, 2017, featuring their Mario Kart 8 Deluxe playthrough, the two hosts race against each other on a specific track starting at the two-minute timestamp. As of June 7, 2023, what was the world record time on that same track in the game's 150cc mode? Provide your answer in minutes and seconds, with seconds rounded to the nearest hundredth (for instance, 1:01.001).", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: At the two-minute mark in the YouTube video uploaded by the channel “GameGrumps” on May 14, 2017 as part of their playthrough of the game Mario Kart 8\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text<tool_calls:6124c78e>\nGameGrumps May 14 2017 Mario Kart 8 Deluxe YouTube 2:00 track</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\nLesson: The search queries remained too broad (channel+date+game only, then +timestamp without extracting the actual track name from video metadata/transcript/description), so no track ide", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text</arg_key:6124c78e>\nGameGrumps May 14 2017 Mario Kart 8 Deluxe YouTube video</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "1:41.614", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 745, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 446.69, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 446.69, "prof_tok_in": 497, "prof_tok_out": 219, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:10:48.123806", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Here is the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nYour job is to answer the following question precisely.\n\nQuestion: Among the statements below, exactly one is **not** logically equivalent to the others:\n\n¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nIdentify the full statement that does not belong.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 100%]\nTask: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not lo\nAs recorded: ```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    \"F1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"F2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"F3\": lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not (not B)) or (not A)),  # A->B == ¬B->¬A\n    \"F4\": lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B),  # A->B == ¬A∨B\n    \"F5\": lambda A,B: ((not (not A)) or B) == (A or (not B)),  # ¬A->B == A", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\nstatements = {\n    \"1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"3\": lambda A,B: ( (not A) or B ) == ( (not (not B)) or (not A) ),  # (A->B) <-> (¬B->¬A)\n    \"4\": lambda A,B: ( (not A) or B ) == ( (not A) or B ),              # (A->B) <-> (¬A∨B)\n    \"5\": lambda A,B: ( (not (not A)) or B ) == ( A or (not B) ),        # (¬A->B) <-> (A∨¬B) as written? Wait compute directly:\n    \"6\": lambda A,B: ( not ( (not A) or B ) ) == ( A and (not B) ),     # ¬(A->B) <-> (A∧¬B)\n}\n\n# Actually compute statement 5 directly from symbols: (¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\ndef stmt5(A,B):\n    left = (not (not A)) or B   # ¬A → B = A ∨ B\n    right = A or (not B)\n    return left == right\n\nfor name, fn in statements.items():\n    if name == \"5\":\n        fn = stmt5\n    results = [fn(A,B) for A,B in itertools.product([True,False], repeat=2)]\n    print(name, results, all(results))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 678, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 547.94, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 547.94, "prof_tok_in": 634, "prof_tok_out": 1774, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:10:48.123990", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7b5377b0-3f38-4103-8ad2-90fe89864c04", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded task:\n\n---\n\n**Question:** Solve for x, rounding your answer to the nearest tenth:\n\nLx = (d/dx × (A × x²)) + 4,097 − C\n\nwhere:\n\n- L = the final two digits of the year in which Venezuela declared independence,\n- A = the count of colors found in the TikTok logo as of July 2023, not counting black or white,\n- C = the mean height of a woman in the Philippines, in centimeters rounded to the nearest whole number, as reported in a Business Insider article from July 2023.\n\n---", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 100%]\nTask: Find the value of x to the nearest tenth: Lx = (d/dx * (A * x-squared)) + 4-thousand'n'ninety-7 minus C\nWhere L is the last two digits of the year of \nAs recorded: </think:6124c78e>I'll research each component needed for the equation.\n\n**Step 1: Find L (last two digits of Venezuelan Declaration of Independence year)**</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Venezuelan Declaration of Independence year</text></query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Venezuelan Declaration of Independence year</text></query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>TikTok logo colors cyan magenta count excluding black white</text></query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Business Insider July 2023 average height woman Philippines centimeters</text></query>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "563.9", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 677, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 378.31, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 378.31, "prof_tok_in": 487, "prof_tok_out": 556, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
