{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:22:13.570921", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_56db2318-640f-477a-a82f-bc93ad13e882", "task_desc": "The following numbers operate similarly to ISBN-13 numbers but with a different validation scheme. Instead of alternating weights of 1 and 3, the checksum digit uses a weight of 1 alternating with some other positive integer below 10. Apart from that, the checksum digit is computed in the usual way. Unfortunately, the data contains an error: two adjacent columns have been swapped. The swapped columns do not involve the last column nor any of the first three columns. Using this information, deter", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 8/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: The following numbers operate like ISBN-13 codes but with a modified validation scheme. In\nAs recorded: ```python\nnumbers = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\n\nsolutions = []\nfor x in range(2, 10):\n    for y in range(3, 11):  \nLesson: Exhaustive nested enumeration over the discrete unknown weight range (2-9) and admissible adjacent-swap starting indices (3-10) combined with an in-place column restoration before ", "response": "```python\nnumbers = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\"\n]\n\nsolutions = []\nfor x in range(2, 10):\n    for y in range(3, 11):  # y smaller index, 3..10 inclusive\n        ok = True\n        for s in numbers:\n            digits = list(map(int, s))\n            # swap columns y and y+1\n            digits[y], digits[y+1] = digits[y+1], digits[y]\n            total = 0\n            for i, d in enumerate(digits):\n                w = 1 if i % 2 == 0 else x\n                total += d * w\n            if total % 10 != 0:\n                ok = False\n                break\n        if ok:\n            solutions.append((x, y))\nsolutions\n```", "expected": "7, 9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 706, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 350.59, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 350.59, "prof_tok_in": 658, "prof_tok_out": 1439, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:22:38.716743", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_6b078778-0b90-464d-83f6-59511c811b01", "task_desc": "The Metropolitan Museum of Art holds a portrait identified by accession number 29.100.5. Among all the consecrators and co-consecrators who elevated this portrait's subject to the office of bishop, which one never ascended to the papacy? Provide that individual's name.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: The Metropolitan Museum of Art has a portrait in its collection with an accession number of 29.100.5. Of the consecrators and co-consecrators of this \nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Metropolitan Museum of Art 29.100.5 portrait</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Metropolitan Museum of Art 29.100.5 portrait</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Alfonso Visconti", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 475, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 528.75, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 528.75, "prof_tok_in": 375, "prof_tok_out": 111, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
