{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:23:24.909453", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_840bfca7-4f7b-481a-8794-c560c340185d", "task_desc": "On June 6, 2023, Universe Today featured an article by Carolyn Collins Petersen. Within that piece, she references a research team and their observational study, with a link to the corresponding paper provided at the end of the article. Locate that paper. What NASA award number supported the work of R. G. Arendt?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: Carolyn Collins Petersen authored an article that appeared in Universe Today on June 6, 20\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Universe Today Carolyn Collins Petersen June 6 2023 observations paper</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>text>Universe Today Carolyn Collins Petersen June 6 2023 observations paper</text>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "80GSFC21M0002", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 441, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 528.75, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 528.75, "prof_tok_in": 375, "prof_tok_out": 143, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:23:24.909595", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Please answer the following question precisely.\n\nQuestion: Per World Bank data, for each year from 2001 through 2010, which nations maintained gross savings exceeding 35% of their GDP? Provide your response as a comma-separated list, sorted alphabetically, using each country's most common English name.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: Per World Bank data, during each individual year from 2001 through 2010, which countries m\nAs recorded: ```python\nimport requests, json, time, sys\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\ndate = \"2001:2010\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"date\": date, \"format\": \"json\", \"per_page\": 1000, \"page\": 1}\n\nall_data = []\npage = 1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"] = page\n   ", "response": "```python\nimport requests, time, json\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICTR.ZS\"\ndate = \"2001:2010\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}\"\nparams = {\"format\":\"json\",\"per_page\":1000,\"page\":1,\"date\":date}\nall_rows = []\npage=1\nwhile True:\n    params[\"page\"]=page\n    r=requests.get(url,params=params,timeout=30)\n    data=r.json()\n    if len(data)<2 or data[1] is None:\n        break\n    all_rows.extend(data[1])\n    if len(data[1])<1000:\n        break\n    page+=1\n    time.sleep(0.2)\nlen(all_rows)\n```\n\n```python\n# Inspect structure and unique countries\nsample = all_rows[0]\nsample\n```\n\n```python\n# Build dict: country -> {year: value}\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ndata_by_country = defaultdict(dict)\ncountry_name_wb = {}\nfor row in all_rows:\n    c = row['country']['value']\n    iso = row['countryiso3code']\n    year = int(row['date'])\n    val = row['value']\n    country_name_wb[iso] = c\n    if val is not None:\n        data_by_country[iso][year] = val\n# years needed\nyears = list(range(2001,2011))\n# countries with >35 in all years\nqualifying = []\nfor iso, yv in data_by_country.items():\n    if all(year in yv and yv[year] > 35 for year in years):\n        qualifying.append(iso)\nlen(qualifying), qualifying[:10]\n```\n\n```python\n# Get WB names for qualifying\n[(iso, country_name_wb[iso]) for iso in qualifying]\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also check if any country missing some year but >35 in available? We'll just focus on all years.\n# Print values for these to verify\nfor iso in qualifying:\n    print(iso, country_name_wb[iso], [data_by_country[iso][y] for y in years])\n```\n\n```python\n# Map to common English names\nmapping = {\n    'ARE':'United Arab Emirates',\n    'AZE':'Azerbaijan',\n    'BHR':'Bahrain',\n    'BRN':'Brunei',\n    'CHN':'China',\n    'COD':'DR Congo',\n    'COM':'Comoros',\n    'GNQ':'Equatorial Guinea',\n    'GAB':'Gabon',\n    'IRN':'Iran',\n    'IRQ':'Iraq',\n    'KAZ':'Kazakhstan',\n    'KWT':'Kuwait',\n    'LAO':'Laos',\n    'LBY':'Libya',\n    'MRT':'Mauritania',\n    'MYA':'Myanmar',\n    'OMN':'Oman',\n    'QAT':'Qatar',\n    'RUS':'Russia',\n    'SAU':'Saudi Arabia',\n    'SUR':'Suriname',\n    'SYR':'Syria',\n    'TKM':'Turkmenistan',\n    'UZB':'Uzbekistan',\n    'VEN':'Venezuela',\n    'VNM':'Vietnam',\n    'YEM':'Yemen',\n    'ZMB':'Zambia',\n    'KGZ':'Kyrgyzstan',\n    'TZA':'Tanzania',\n    'TLS':'Timor-Leste',\n    'SDN':'Sudan',\n    'ERI':'Eritrea',\n    'GIN':'Guinea',\n    'MOZ':'Mozambique',\n    'ETH':'Ethiopia',\n    'BOL':'Bolivia',\n    'ECU':'Ecuador',\n    'COL':'Colombia',\n    'PER':'Peru',\n    'GTM':'Guatemala',\n    'SLV':'El Salvador',\n    'HND':'Honduras',\n    'DOM':'Dominican Republic',\n    'PAN':'Panama',\n    'CRI':'Costa Rica',\n    'JAM':'Jamaica',\n    'TTO':'Trinidad and Tobago',\n    'MNG':'Mongolia',\n    'NPL':'Nepal',\n    'BTN':'Bh