{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:23:37.474763", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_8d46b8d6-b38a-47ff-ac74-cda14cf2d19b", "task_desc": "Based on the upper estimates found on English Wikipedia at the close of 2012, what fraction of the overall penguin population is represented by the penguins in this file that either do not reside on Dream Island or possess beaks exceeding 42mm in length? Provide your answer as a percentage rounded to five decimal places.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: What percentage of the total penguin population according to the upper estimates on englis\nAs recorded: </think:6124c78e>I'll start by exploring the environment to find the referenced file and then search for the Wikipedia population estimate.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os, sys, glob\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\nprint('---')\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.s\n\n## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: Here's the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nBased on the upper population estimates from the Englis\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): ```python\nimport os\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.startswith('.'):\n            print(os.path.join(root, ", "response": "```python\nimport os\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.startswith('.'):\n            print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```\n\n```python\nimport os\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        if not f.startswith('.'):\n            print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "0.00033", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 897, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 675.76, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 675.76, "prof_tok_in": 494, "prof_tok_out": 465, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:23:37.524508", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Among the following, identify the one statement that is not logically equivalent to the others:\n\n¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above does not belong? Give the complete statement that differs.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 100%]\nTask: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) \nAs recorded: ```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    \"F1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"F2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"F3\": lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not (not B)) or (not A)),  # A->B == ¬B->¬A\n    \"F4\": lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not A\n\n## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: Among the statements below, exactly one is **not** logically equivalent to the others:\n\n¬(\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): ```python\nimport itertools\n\nstatements = {\n    \"1\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"2\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not ", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef f1(A,B): return (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\ndef f2(A,B): return (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\ndef f3(A,B): return ((A implies B) == ((not B) implies (not A)))  # need define implies\ndef impl(p,q): return (not p) or q\n\ndef f3(A,B): return impl(A,B) == impl(not B, not A)\ndef f4(A,B): return impl(A,B) == (impl(not A,B))? Wait (¬A ∨ B) is impl(A,B). So f4: impl(A,B) == ((not A) or B) which is same as impl(A,B) == impl(A,B) tautology.\ndef f5(A,B): return impl(not A, B) == (A or (not B))\ndef f6(A,B): return (not impl(A,B)) == (A and (not B))\n\nLet's just code.\n```</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef impl(p,q):\n    return (not p) or q\n\nformulas = {\n    \"1: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\": lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    \"2: ¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\": lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    \"3: (A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\": lambda A,B: impl(A,B) == impl(not B, not A),\n    \"4: (A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\": lambda A,B: impl(A,B) == ((not A) or B),\n    \"5: (¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\": lambda A,B: impl(not A, B) == (A or (not B)),\n    \"6: ¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\": lambda A,B: (not impl(A,B)) == (A and (not B)),\n}\n\nfor name,f in formulas.items():\n    results = [f(A,B) for A in [True,False] for B in [True,False]]\n    print(name, results, all(results))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 899, "wc_served": [0.85, 0.85], "wc_mean": 0.85, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 675.76, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 675.76, "prof_tok_in": 646, "prof_tok_out": 817, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
