{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:23:38.821132", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_708b99c5-e4a7-49cb-a5cf-933c8d46470d", "task_desc": "Here's the reworded variant:\n\n---\n\nFor the DeepFruits fruit detection graph on Connected Papers dating from 2016, which attribute determined the size of the largest bubble on that graph?", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 0%]\nTask: On the DeepFruits fruit detection graph on Connected Papers from 2016, what feature caused\nAs recorded: <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_response:6124c78e>\n# Search Results\n1. [How to use Connected Papers? - Connected Papers Help Center](https://help.connectedpapers.com/how-to-use-connected-papers)\n2. [Connect\n\n## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: Here's the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nOn the 2016 DeepFruits fruit detection graph displayed \nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): <tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>text_quer", "response": "<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_response:6124c78e>\n<think:6124c78e>The search didn't return results? The previous tool call seems malformed? Actually I sent web_search with empty query? Wait I used `<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>` with no content? The result shows no output? Let's re-issue properly.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>\n<arg_key:6124c78e><think:6124c78e>The tool call seems to have not executed? The previous response shows no search results, maybe because I didn't close tags properly. Let's do a proper search.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>\n<arg_key:6124c78e><think:6124c78e>It seems my tool calls are not being executed properly. The system shows \"You are an expert research assistant...\" and then I attempted to call web_search but the format may be wrong. The expected format is:\n\n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\n<query content>\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\n```\n\nWait, the instructions show using `<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>` then the query text then `</tool_call:6124c78e>`. Actually the correct syntax in this environment: The tool name is `web_search`, and it has a parameter `query`. The format used in the prompt's prior attempts: \n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_response:6124c78e>\n# Search Results\n...\n```\nBut that seems they put `<query>` as a nested tag? Actually they wrote:\n```\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query<tool_call:6124c78e>\n<tool_response:6124c78e>\n```\nThat is malformed. The proper way: \n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\nDeepFruits Connected Papers bubble size\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n```\nNo, the parameter is inside the tool call. Let's look at typical format: \n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\n\"DeepFruits\" \"Connected Papers\" bubble size\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\n```\nBut the `query` tag should enclose the query string. Let's try:\n\n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\nConnected Papers node size attribute\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\n```\n\nWait, the tool call block should be:\n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\nConnected Papers node size attribute\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\n```\nBut there is an extra `<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>` inside? Actually the tool call itself has parameters, and the parameter tag is `query`. So:\n```\n<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\nConnected Papers node size attribute\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>\n```\nThis might be correct: The outer tag is `tool_use`? No, the system says use `<tool_call:6124c78e>tool_name<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>param_name</tool_call:6124c78e>\nparam_value\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n`. So yes.\n\nLet's do that.</think:6124c78e><tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>web_search<tool_calls:6124c78e>\n<tool_call:6124c78e>query</tool_call:6124c78e>\nConnected Papers node size attribute largest bubble\n</tool_call:6124c78e>\n</tool_calls:6124c78e>", "expected": "Citations", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 897, "wc_served": [0.95, 0.95], "wc_mean": 0.95, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 675.76, "prof_emb