{"timestamp": "2026-07-22T17:23:40.548653", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nHere's a Boggle board I've set up:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nWhat's the longest English word you can form from this board? I want to know the longest word that can be generated from it. If there's a tie at the maximum length, give me the one that sorts first alphabetically. And since different Boggle word lists exist, let's stick to the words_alpha dictionary hosted at https://github.com/dwyl/english-words as our official word source.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[✓ Prior attempt — curator quality 5/10, self-assessed 50%]\nTask: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\n\nAs recorded: ```python\nimport urllib.request, bisect, time\n\nurl = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt'\nprint('Downloading dictionary...')\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwords = [w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip().isalpha()\n\n## What to avoid (from earlier attempts)\n\n[✗ Earlier attempt fell short]\nTask: I've been asked to reword the task, so here is the reworded version:\n\n---\n\nUsing the Boggl\nAs recorded (self-assessed doubtful, verify before reuse): ```python\nimport urllib.request\n\nurl = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt'\nprint('Downloading dictionary...'", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, bisect, time\n\nurl = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt'\nprint('Downloading dictionary...')\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwords = sorted(w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip().isalpha())\nprint('Dictionary size:', len(words))\n\n# Boggle board 4x4\nboard = [\n    'A','B','R','L',\n    'E','I','T','E',\n    'I','O','N','S',\n    'F','P','E','I'\n]\n\n# Precompute neighbors (king moves)\nneighbors = [[] for _ in range(16)]\nfor i in range(16):\n    r, c = divmod(i, 4)\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0 <= nr < 4 and 0 <= nc < 4:\n                j = nr*4 + nc\n                neighbors[i].append(j)\n\ndef is_prefix(s):\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(words, s)\n    if idx < len(words) and words[idx].startswith(s):\n        return True, (idx < len(words) and words[idx] == s)\n    return False, False\n\nmax_len = 0\nbest = set()\n\ndef dfs(i, mask, s):\n    global max_len, best\n    ok, exact = is_prefix(s)\n    if not ok:\n        return\n    if exact:\n        if len(s) > max_len:\n            max_len = len(s)\n            best = {s}\n        elif len(s) == max_len:\n            best.add(s)\n    for j in neighbors[i]:\n        if not (mask & (1 << j)):\n            dfs(j, mask | (1 << j), s + board[j])\n\nfor i in range(16):\n    dfs(i, 1 << i, board[i])\n\nprint('Max length:', max_len)\nprint('Number of best words:', len(best))\nprint('Best words (sorted):', sorted(best)[:20])\nprint('Alphabetically first:', sorted(best)[0])\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 898, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": true, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "b0e4cf06", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "7cb32d15a57d", "prof_total_s": 621.77, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 621.77, "prof_tok_in": 561, "prof_tok_out": 3792, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
